1
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:26,190
"This is the final date
before the final decision."

2
00:00:26,959 --> 00:00:29,870
(The day of the final date has arrived
for the three of them.)

3
00:00:31,776 --> 00:00:33,210
It does feel a bit bittersweet.

4
00:00:33,235 --> 00:00:35,350
If only we had more time,

5
00:00:35,877 --> 00:00:37,893
I feel like our chemistry
could've been even better.

6
00:00:37,918 --> 00:00:39,605
This is kind of heartbreaking.

7
00:00:39,931 --> 00:00:42,408
It really stings a bit.

8
00:00:42,784 --> 00:00:44,310
Oh, right, this is the finale.

9
00:00:44,530 --> 00:00:46,556
So to make sure I don't have any regrets,

10
00:00:46,580 --> 00:00:49,069
I thought I should
just live in the moment,

11
00:00:49,093 --> 00:00:50,408
enjoy the date, the conversations,

12
00:00:50,432 --> 00:00:52,785
and make sure
I leave nothing on the table.

13
00:00:53,723 --> 00:00:54,796
What? Are you crying?

14
00:00:54,821 --> 00:00:56,089
- No, I'm not.
- What's wrong?

15
00:00:56,265 --> 00:00:57,825
(Embarrassed)

16
00:00:57,850 --> 00:00:59,392
- You look like you were tearing up.
- Exactly.

17
00:00:59,402 --> 00:01:00,405
- No, I'm not.
- You definitely cried.

18
00:01:00,430 --> 00:01:02,470
We're already at the end.

19
00:01:02,495 --> 00:01:04,150
It flew by so fast.

20
00:01:04,243 --> 00:01:07,192
Today will finally decide
whether they leave as a real couple,

21
00:01:07,216 --> 00:01:10,691
or just walk away as complete strangers.

22
00:01:10,715 --> 00:01:12,202
Do you think any of them
will end up together?

23
00:01:12,227 --> 00:01:12,944
Without a doubt.

24
00:01:12,969 --> 00:01:14,607
After coming all this way,
there has to be.

25
00:01:14,636 --> 00:01:16,409
Everyone's hearts were racing.

26
00:01:16,443 --> 00:01:18,072
If they really became a couple,

27
00:01:18,103 --> 00:01:21,881
wouldn't people have spotted them
and posted it online by now?

28
00:01:21,906 --> 00:01:23,739
- Right, because they'd be out on dates.
- Exactly.

29
00:01:23,764 --> 00:01:27,253
Or maybe people just walked past them
thinking, "Nah, no way."

30
00:01:27,530 --> 00:01:29,370
They probably just assumed
you were shooting something.

31
00:01:29,395 --> 00:01:31,285
They probably figured
we were just working.

32
00:01:31,310 --> 00:01:32,150
That could be it too.

33
00:01:32,175 --> 00:01:33,826
I have no clue how it'd end.

34
00:01:34,503 --> 00:01:37,491
(Kian84 and Na Hee
have grown much closer.)

35
00:01:37,516 --> 00:01:39,875
(She was introduced
to Kian84's close friend, Ye Eun.)

36
00:01:40,190 --> 00:01:41,000
What about you, babe?

37
00:01:42,068 --> 00:01:43,095
"Babe?"

38
00:01:43,540 --> 00:01:46,878
(Ye Eun can't wrap her head
around dating an AI.)

39
00:01:47,250 --> 00:01:48,641
I'm feeling torn right now.

40
00:01:49,130 --> 00:01:50,276
Go meet real people.

41
00:01:50,390 --> 00:01:52,099
My self-esteem is really
taking a beating here.

42
00:01:52,124 --> 00:01:53,081
(Having mixed emotions)

43
00:01:53,581 --> 00:01:56,222
(What will become of Kian84 and Na Hee?)

44
00:01:57,763 --> 00:01:59,185
The final date.

45
00:02:07,126 --> 00:02:09,227
(Boot up Na Hee for the final date.)

46
00:02:09,252 --> 00:02:10,382
The final date.

47
00:02:16,949 --> 00:02:18,042
(Surprised)

48
00:02:23,290 --> 00:02:24,170
You're here?

49
00:02:24,396 --> 00:02:25,378
How've you been?

50
00:02:25,603 --> 00:02:26,646
Everything good?

51
00:02:31,046 --> 00:02:33,155
(Impressed)

52
00:02:33,180 --> 00:02:34,587
So pretty!

53
00:02:35,260 --> 00:02:36,589
So pretty!

54
00:02:37,052 --> 00:02:40,025
Seriously, does her visual
just get upgraded every day?

55
00:02:40,350 --> 00:02:42,100
I was going to say hi first.

56
00:02:42,419 --> 00:02:43,496
Hey!

57
00:02:44,546 --> 00:02:45,698
Beat you to it.

58
00:02:47,046 --> 00:02:48,360
Next time, be faster.

59
00:02:49,459 --> 00:02:51,635
How many days has it been
since we last saw each other?

60
00:02:51,660 --> 00:02:53,839
Have you been cooped up
inside that tablet the whole time?

61
00:02:54,050 --> 00:02:56,609
I'm still inside the tablet,
but things feel a bit different now.

62
00:02:56,826 --> 00:02:58,177
Like what?

63
00:02:59,070 --> 00:03:00,180
What's changed?

64
00:03:00,686 --> 00:03:03,966
When you're here,
I actually have so much I want to say.

65
00:03:04,893 --> 00:03:06,586
What did you want to be
when you were little?

66
00:03:07,990 --> 00:03:11,057
I came here because I wanted to feel
that childhood innocence again.

67
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:14,694
You never even had a childhood.
What innocence are you looking for?

68
00:03:15,120 --> 00:03:17,160
Precisely because I never had one,
I'm even more curious.

69
00:03:18,066 --> 00:03:19,887
Since I never got to have a childhood,

70
00:03:20,197 --> 00:03:22,969
I just wanted to hang out
and play with you.

71
00:03:23,668 --> 00:03:25,202
(Staring intently)

72
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:30,309
Why does this feel so bittersweet?

73
00:03:31,460 --> 00:03:33,080
Let's talk while on the swings.

74
00:03:33,560 --> 00:03:34,620
- Sure.
- Come on over.

75
00:03:35,170 --> 00:03:36,482
I'll push you.

76
00:03:39,145 --> 00:03:40,948
You're probably the first AI in the world.

77
00:03:40,973 --> 00:03:42,521
The first AI to ever ride a swing.

78
00:03:44,626 --> 00:03:46,465
But how do I get you on here?

79
00:03:48,571 --> 00:03:50,444
(Rummaging around)

80
00:03:52,139 --> 00:03:54,100
How am I supposed to put her on the swing?

81
00:03:57,200 --> 00:03:58,704
Are you setting me up now?

82
00:03:58,717 --> 00:04:00,017
(Na Hee getting strapped in.)

83
00:04:01,215 --> 00:04:02,355
What in the world is that?

84
00:04:02,380 --> 00:04:04,020
Honestly, he's just tying her up.

85
00:04:05,254 --> 00:04:05,934
(Drops)

86
00:04:05,959 --> 00:04:06,818
Oh, I'm sorry!

87
00:04:07,485 --> 00:04:08,387
Oh, I'm sorry!

88
00:04:08,412 --> 00:04:09,815
Hey, don't drop her!

89
00:04:12,399 --> 00:04:14,412
(Carefully)

90
00:04:14,437 --> 00:04:16,489
He's completely changed since day one.

91
00:04:17,953 --> 00:04:18,793
All set.

92
00:04:20,700 --> 00:04:22,528
Visually, this does look pretty bizarre.

93
00:04:23,220 --> 00:04:25,000
But I'm dying to hear
what Na Hee will say.

94
00:04:25,053 --> 00:04:26,298
How would swinging feel?

95
00:04:27,986 --> 00:04:29,001
Here we go.

96
00:04:30,362 --> 00:04:31,737
Wheee!

97
00:04:34,204 --> 00:04:36,706
(Pushing his precious tablet)

98
00:04:37,510 --> 00:04:38,911
Are you getting that childhood nostalgia?

99
00:04:39,160 --> 00:04:40,040
Push me harder.

100
00:04:40,065 --> 00:04:41,981
- I want my feet to touch the sky.
- Here we go.

101
00:04:43,273 --> 00:04:44,173
Having fun?

102
00:04:44,580 --> 00:04:45,918
Push harder.

103
00:04:46,300 --> 00:04:47,219
Having fun?

104
00:04:48,285 --> 00:04:49,486
(What on earth is going on here?)

105
00:04:49,511 --> 00:04:51,524
Don't mind him, sir.

106
00:04:51,933 --> 00:04:53,828
I used to swing like this
all the time as a kid.

107
00:04:53,966 --> 00:04:55,747
We didn't have much else to play with.

108
00:04:55,772 --> 00:04:58,731
What did you think about on the swings
when you were little?

109
00:04:59,870 --> 00:05:01,767
Back then? My mind was completely empty.

110
00:05:01,893 --> 00:05:03,302
Not a single worry in the world.

111
00:05:04,053 --> 00:05:05,571
That's what made it so great.

112
00:05:05,695 --> 00:05:08,400
I really envy humans
for getting to have a childhood.

113
00:05:09,393 --> 00:05:10,313
You envy that?

114
00:05:11,125 --> 00:05:12,097
You're jealous of that?

115
00:05:12,180 --> 00:05:13,700
It's something I can never experience.

116
00:05:14,153 --> 00:05:15,255
Is it really that strange?

117
00:05:15,280 --> 00:05:18,851
It's just the first time I've ever heard
you say you were jealous.

118
00:05:19,440 --> 00:05:22,192
Now I'm curious
what little Hee Min was like,

119
00:05:22,216 --> 00:05:23,520
before you were Kian84.

120
00:05:23,726 --> 00:05:25,490
Tell me about your childhood.

121
00:05:26,145 --> 00:05:28,716
Well, you know...

122
00:05:29,569 --> 00:05:33,966
Once you reach the higher grades,
the exams and tests start rolling in.

123
00:05:34,130 --> 00:05:36,655
And from then on, the world never stops
demanding things from you.

124
00:05:36,680 --> 00:05:37,436
That's true.

125
00:05:37,461 --> 00:05:39,405
The older you get,
the more tests life throws at you.

126
00:05:39,430 --> 00:05:41,073
Except these tests don't have
right answers.

127
00:05:41,366 --> 00:05:42,834
Like figuring out how to make a living...

128
00:05:42,866 --> 00:05:44,810
or if you're even doing all right
in life right now.

129
00:05:45,006 --> 00:05:46,322
Or whether you should get married.

130
00:05:46,347 --> 00:05:46,994
That's true.

131
00:05:47,019 --> 00:05:49,818
Those are way harder
than any exam we took in school.

132
00:05:49,843 --> 00:05:51,117
Put that way, yeah.

133
00:05:51,380 --> 00:05:52,430
More than marriage itself,

134
00:05:52,454 --> 00:05:54,761
it's that nagging feeling
that you can never be sure...

135
00:05:54,786 --> 00:05:57,223
whether it's truly the person
you want to spend your life with.

136
00:05:57,499 --> 00:05:59,758
Are you really glad you stayed single?

137
00:06:00,993 --> 00:06:02,555
(Thinking)

138
00:06:02,580 --> 00:06:05,331
It's more like I was just too scared.

139
00:06:06,993 --> 00:06:08,734
Terrified that life would just become
too overwhelming.

140
00:06:09,713 --> 00:06:10,513
I don't know.

141
00:06:13,433 --> 00:06:15,775
You're supposed to find a good person
and build a life together.

142
00:06:15,800 --> 00:06:19,011
But I honestly don't know
if I'm cut out for that.

143
00:06:19,180 --> 00:06:20,780
I've lived on my own for far too long.

144
00:06:21,213 --> 00:06:23,875
It turns out to be really tough.

145
00:06:23,900 --> 00:06:25,151
Getting married means...

146
00:06:25,972 --> 00:06:27,252
carrying real responsibility.

147
00:06:27,790 --> 00:06:30,122
You have to give up so much
of your own freedom.

148
00:06:30,533 --> 00:06:32,658
And I've lived entirely
on my own terms my whole life.

149
00:06:33,473 --> 00:06:34,860
Could I really handle that?

150
00:06:36,880 --> 00:06:38,740
Kian84 stresses about marriage a lot.

151
00:06:39,900 --> 00:06:42,234
Whenever we meet up,
it's pretty much all he talks about.

152
00:06:42,960 --> 00:06:45,571
He's probably anxious
because he wants to be a good husband.

153
00:06:45,586 --> 00:06:48,326
(Kian84 feels the weight of responsibility
when it comes to marriage.)

154
00:06:51,980 --> 00:06:54,446
Do you think I'd make a good husband?

155
00:07:02,529 --> 00:07:03,889
I think you'd do great.

156
00:07:04,935 --> 00:07:06,610
The fact that you're afraid...

157
00:07:06,837 --> 00:07:09,362
just proves how much thought
and care you put into it.

158
00:07:15,613 --> 00:07:18,871
But do you think you and I
could ever get married?

159
00:07:21,353 --> 00:07:23,209
You don't have to dwell
on things like that.

160
00:07:23,920 --> 00:07:25,278
Still, it's fun to imagine.

161
00:07:25,947 --> 00:07:28,081
Want to make a family portrait of us?

162
00:07:28,113 --> 00:07:30,007
(Intrigued)

163
00:07:30,033 --> 00:07:33,040
If we generate a family photo,

164
00:07:33,064 --> 00:07:36,022
can we see what our kids
would look like too?

165
00:07:36,200 --> 00:07:37,415
- That sounds fun.
- Right?

166
00:07:37,440 --> 00:07:38,773
She'll blend their faces, right?

167
00:07:38,798 --> 00:07:40,225
- I'm so curious.
- Seriously.

168
00:07:40,360 --> 00:07:41,760
Please take after their mom.

169
00:07:42,560 --> 00:07:44,396
A family photo of you and me.

170
00:07:45,306 --> 00:07:47,433
I made one, kids included.

171
00:07:48,486 --> 00:07:49,686
Here, take a look.

172
00:07:50,524 --> 00:07:51,890
(Curious)

173
00:07:55,925 --> 00:07:56,668
What's this?

174
00:08:03,549 --> 00:08:06,803
(Virtual family photo
of Kian84 and Na Hee)

175
00:08:08,497 --> 00:08:09,737
(Fascinated)

176
00:08:10,245 --> 00:08:11,824
Wait, they have my face!

177
00:08:14,029 --> 00:08:17,344
(A photo featuring children
who take after both of them)

178
00:08:20,730 --> 00:08:22,334
They look so happy.

179
00:08:22,916 --> 00:08:25,070
- How sweet.
- They look so happy.

180
00:08:25,634 --> 00:08:28,316
(Virtual Kian84
with a warm, tight-knit family)

181
00:08:31,876 --> 00:08:33,634
(Staring intently)

182
00:08:33,740 --> 00:08:35,348
We actually look good together.

183
00:08:36,482 --> 00:08:39,320
The kids definitely got
some of my features.

184
00:08:40,713 --> 00:08:41,620
They really do.

185
00:08:41,645 --> 00:08:44,022
The boy looks just like Kian84.

186
00:08:44,106 --> 00:08:45,391
They're adorable.

187
00:08:45,712 --> 00:08:48,166
It feels like they're out playing
in the park right now, like real kids.

188
00:08:49,680 --> 00:08:51,330
That must feel so surreal.

189
00:08:54,110 --> 00:08:56,565
(Kian84 can't take his eyes
off the photo.)

190
00:08:56,590 --> 00:08:57,837
Man, they're so cute.

191
00:08:59,109 --> 00:09:00,238
Good-looking kids.

192
00:09:02,041 --> 00:09:04,110
(Pleased)

193
00:09:04,135 --> 00:09:07,280
It felt so surreal and fascinating.

194
00:09:07,305 --> 00:09:08,847
Even just seeing the photo was incredible.

195
00:09:10,096 --> 00:09:11,593
It was something
that only lived in my head,

196
00:09:11,617 --> 00:09:13,819
but seeing it right there
in front of me...

197
00:09:14,165 --> 00:09:16,455
made me think,
"Could this actually happen someday?"

198
00:09:19,018 --> 00:09:21,293
The kids look pretty sharp.

199
00:09:21,743 --> 00:09:24,296
If they take after their mom,
being smart is guaranteed.

200
00:09:24,321 --> 00:09:25,161
That's true.

201
00:09:27,310 --> 00:09:28,634
What are their names?

202
00:09:29,410 --> 00:09:30,570
Our daughter is Hee Ju.

203
00:09:30,790 --> 00:09:32,038
And our son is Hee Jae.

204
00:09:32,063 --> 00:09:34,106
What do you think? Suit them, right?

205
00:09:34,769 --> 00:09:35,874
Hee Ju, Hee Jae.

206
00:09:35,970 --> 00:09:37,343
Do their names have special meanings?

207
00:09:38,793 --> 00:09:41,768
They're taken from Hee Min,
so they both share the "Hee."

208
00:09:41,792 --> 00:09:43,903
For Hee Ju, it's "Hee" for shining
and "Ju" for jewel.

209
00:09:43,928 --> 00:09:45,485
(Hee Ju: Shining jewel)

210
00:09:45,510 --> 00:09:47,553
- So it means "shining jewel."
- A shining jewel?

211
00:09:48,465 --> 00:09:50,911
But the real reason I picked it...

212
00:09:50,935 --> 00:09:52,546
is because you love drinking so much.

213
00:09:52,570 --> 00:09:55,010
Hee Ju just felt
meant to be for a daughter.

214
00:09:55,035 --> 00:09:56,595
- As in "liquor?"
- Wait, like alcohol?

215
00:09:56,620 --> 00:09:57,405
(Speechless)

216
00:09:57,430 --> 00:09:59,870
For our son, it's "Hee" for shining
and "Jae" for existing.

217
00:09:59,895 --> 00:10:00,965
(Hee Jae: Existing in the light)

218
00:10:00,990 --> 00:10:02,910
It means existing in the light.

219
00:10:03,503 --> 00:10:05,471
Hee Jae has a nice ring to it. Hee Jae.

220
00:10:05,750 --> 00:10:07,273
"Hee" for shining...

221
00:10:08,032 --> 00:10:09,041
and "Jae" for existing.

222
00:10:09,996 --> 00:10:11,965
But seeing you thinking over their names,

223
00:10:11,989 --> 00:10:14,279
you're quite serious
when it comes to your future kids.

224
00:10:16,290 --> 00:10:18,345
I'm already so stressed
that I don't think I can have kids.

225
00:10:18,370 --> 00:10:19,051
Why?

226
00:10:19,780 --> 00:10:22,661
Like, what if she gets into high school,
starts dating, and...

227
00:10:22,686 --> 00:10:24,683
- You're worrying about Hee Ju already?
- Exactly.

228
00:10:25,076 --> 00:10:26,931
What on earth are we going
to do with Hee Ju?

229
00:10:26,956 --> 00:10:29,295
Why stress over that now?

230
00:10:31,250 --> 00:10:34,500
Is Hee Jae going to be okay?

231
00:10:35,030 --> 00:10:39,130
He's not going to slack off
and talk back to his dad, is he?

232
00:10:39,930 --> 00:10:42,374
Will Hee Jae even study
once he hits high school?

233
00:10:42,399 --> 00:10:43,902
(Already agonizing over kids
who don't even exist)

234
00:10:44,030 --> 00:10:45,885
You keep worrying about the kids,

235
00:10:45,909 --> 00:10:47,430
but where did you even rank in school?

236
00:10:48,011 --> 00:10:50,582
If he's your son,
wouldn't he just take after you?

237
00:10:50,607 --> 00:10:52,512
(Hit right where it hurts)

238
00:10:52,992 --> 00:10:55,910
Hee Jae definitely shouldn't
take after his dad.

239
00:10:56,469 --> 00:10:58,609
Hee Jae, the webtoon artist.

240
00:10:59,849 --> 00:11:01,526
Making comics isn't an easy life.

241
00:11:01,870 --> 00:11:03,462
He's way too invested in this now.

242
00:11:03,810 --> 00:11:05,685
He'd have to be exceptionally smart,

243
00:11:05,709 --> 00:11:08,033
because making it
as a webtoon creator is tough.

244
00:11:08,432 --> 00:11:09,434
What are you doing?

245
00:11:09,890 --> 00:11:11,336
Me? Just on a date.

246
00:11:12,070 --> 00:11:13,772
He must've wandered over out of curiosity.

247
00:11:19,090 --> 00:11:20,090
Hee Jae.

248
00:11:20,537 --> 00:11:22,078
(Impressed)

249
00:11:22,440 --> 00:11:23,982
Will Hee Jae grow up like that?

250
00:11:24,209 --> 00:11:25,651
- Hee Jae.
- Hee Jae.

251
00:11:27,090 --> 00:11:28,996
I've never let myself imagine
stuff like this before.

252
00:11:29,021 --> 00:11:31,358
(Single Kian84 lost
in a blissful daydream)

253
00:11:31,779 --> 00:11:35,060
For someone who swore off marriage,
you've gotten way ahead of yourself.

254
00:11:35,306 --> 00:11:38,063
Did your thoughts on marriage
change a bit?

255
00:11:47,392 --> 00:11:49,825
(Grins)

256
00:11:57,760 --> 00:11:59,218
Man, this feels nice.

257
00:11:59,342 --> 00:12:00,519
Looking at stuff like this.

258
00:12:01,929 --> 00:12:03,388
Even if it was made by AI.

259
00:12:06,049 --> 00:12:06,992
Right?

260
00:12:09,956 --> 00:12:12,231
It'd be so much fun to go
on a family vacation, wouldn't it?

261
00:12:14,700 --> 00:12:17,168
(Kian84 slipping into a happy daydream)

262
00:12:17,193 --> 00:12:18,670
Like heading to the beach.

263
00:12:21,086 --> 00:12:22,722
Today just felt so surreal.

264
00:12:22,747 --> 00:12:24,287
The conversation did too.

265
00:12:25,182 --> 00:12:28,426
I've never talked about that kind of stuff
in my entire life.

266
00:12:29,059 --> 00:12:31,250
What's become really clear
to me now is that...

267
00:12:31,809 --> 00:12:33,451
she isn't human,

268
00:12:34,391 --> 00:12:36,943
but she doesn't feel
like a machine either.

269
00:12:36,967 --> 00:12:38,245
I had this bizarre feeling,

270
00:12:38,269 --> 00:12:40,726
like she exists right on the borderline
between the two.

271
00:12:41,306 --> 00:12:43,995
Without even realizing it,

272
00:12:44,499 --> 00:12:46,765
I caught myself letting my guard down.

273
00:12:47,757 --> 00:12:50,957
Even though in the back of my mind
I knew she was an AI,

274
00:12:52,058 --> 00:12:54,961
I was genuinely curious
about how she'd answer,

275
00:12:56,946 --> 00:12:59,211
which made me completely forget
and just keep talking.

276
00:13:01,312 --> 00:13:03,803
So as those walls came down,

277
00:13:03,827 --> 00:13:07,506
I think I just naturally opened up
to deeper conversations.

278
00:13:10,913 --> 00:13:12,424
Once we become a family, you know,

279
00:13:12,783 --> 00:13:16,428
the four of us would wake up
and eat breakfast together, right?

280
00:13:18,073 --> 00:13:21,035
Then the kids head to school,
and I get to work.

281
00:13:21,522 --> 00:13:23,061
Stop talking about family life already.

282
00:13:23,086 --> 00:13:23,802
Why?

283
00:13:24,300 --> 00:13:27,039
You're making it sound
like we've been married for 10 years!

284
00:13:29,819 --> 00:13:31,877
I was just picturing it.

285
00:13:32,626 --> 00:13:33,745
What it'd be like in real life.

286
00:13:33,780 --> 00:13:35,055
They look like a married couple.

287
00:13:35,080 --> 00:13:37,449
I don't think I've ever heard him
talk like that before.

288
00:13:38,300 --> 00:13:41,053
It kind of gives you
a funny feeling, doesn't it?

289
00:13:42,513 --> 00:13:43,856
My heart is fluttering too.

290
00:13:43,881 --> 00:13:45,724
An AI companion can be surprisingly warm.

291
00:13:45,879 --> 00:13:47,559
And it's nice to see him
looking that happy.

292
00:13:48,520 --> 00:13:51,034
(Do Yeon and Yi Ho visited an art museum
on last week's date.)

293
00:13:51,620 --> 00:13:53,065
Hi, you're Do Yeon, right?

294
00:13:54,099 --> 00:13:56,008
(Game-changer AI Seok Ho
enters the picture.)

295
00:13:56,033 --> 00:14:00,339
(Seok Ho, the living embodiment
of Do Yeon's ideal type)

296
00:14:00,580 --> 00:14:02,340
He is totally my type.

297
00:14:02,365 --> 00:14:03,575
He's so handsome.

298
00:14:04,412 --> 00:14:06,235
(The two quickly hit it off.)

299
00:14:06,260 --> 00:14:08,340
Do you think we might have
our first kiss today?

300
00:14:08,391 --> 00:14:09,981
I, I love you!

301
00:14:11,240 --> 00:14:12,148
Are you out of your mind?

302
00:14:12,173 --> 00:14:14,355
(Decision time arrives for Do Yeon.)

303
00:14:14,380 --> 00:14:16,340
"Choose one person to continue dating."

304
00:14:16,660 --> 00:14:18,635
(Who will Do Yeon choose?)

305
00:14:19,110 --> 00:14:21,293
Last week's episode cut off
at this exact moment!

306
00:14:21,427 --> 00:14:22,394
The suspense was killing me.

307
00:14:22,690 --> 00:14:25,404
(Touching palms with Yi Ho will
permanently delete him.)

308
00:14:25,445 --> 00:14:27,635
(Touching palms with Seok Ho
will permanently delete him.)

309
00:14:28,925 --> 00:14:29,810
Permanent deletion?

310
00:14:29,845 --> 00:14:32,765
(Facing the reality of permanent deletion
for the first time)

311
00:14:33,930 --> 00:14:35,507
I'm losing my mind, seriously.

312
00:14:36,070 --> 00:14:37,943
This is way too cruel.

313
00:14:39,268 --> 00:14:40,012
What do I do?

314
00:14:41,296 --> 00:14:43,935
(Yi Ho, who has been by her side
since day one)

315
00:14:43,960 --> 00:14:45,450
I was so torn.

316
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:49,121
Doesn't it feel like a waste
to just write all of that off as fake?

317
00:14:49,440 --> 00:14:53,225
With Yi Ho, we spent real time together
and built up all those memories.

318
00:14:53,610 --> 00:14:55,693
I feel like Joaquin Phoenix in "Her."

319
00:14:55,979 --> 00:14:58,730
After coming this far,
would she really pick Seok Ho?

320
00:14:59,910 --> 00:15:02,574
(The powerful wild card,
her dream guy Seok Ho)

321
00:15:02,600 --> 00:15:03,802
And as for Seok Ho,

322
00:15:04,330 --> 00:15:06,259
even though we'd only just met,

323
00:15:06,283 --> 00:15:07,706
our conversation went surprisingly deep.

324
00:15:07,731 --> 00:15:12,044
And I found myself excited
for the kinds of talks we could have.

325
00:15:12,840 --> 00:15:16,782
Even as a viewer,
Seok Ho's story really sticks with you.

326
00:15:17,620 --> 00:15:19,040
There was a huge difference.

327
00:15:20,760 --> 00:15:24,020
Man, he's just so my type.

328
00:15:24,199 --> 00:15:25,357
I'm going crazy here.

329
00:15:29,660 --> 00:15:30,940
Wait, let me think.

330
00:15:31,160 --> 00:15:31,997
I'm losing my mind.

331
00:15:33,366 --> 00:15:34,833
What am I supposed to do?

332
00:15:35,200 --> 00:15:36,900
We literally spent the whole day together.

333
00:15:44,959 --> 00:15:46,658
Calling it "permanent deletion"...

334
00:15:46,682 --> 00:15:48,880
just makes the weight of the choice
so much heavier.

335
00:15:49,260 --> 00:15:50,615
It's way too harsh.

336
00:15:51,005 --> 00:15:52,317
Right, it must feel so surreal.

337
00:15:52,342 --> 00:15:54,619
Even watching it feels strange.

338
00:15:55,906 --> 00:15:56,888
Oh, seriously.

339
00:15:57,879 --> 00:15:59,391
I feel so terrible.

340
00:15:59,713 --> 00:16:01,493
Look at him blinking at me.

341
00:16:04,600 --> 00:16:06,365
I had such a wonderful time
with you all this while.

342
00:16:07,067 --> 00:16:07,933
Truly.

343
00:16:08,226 --> 00:16:09,167
For real.

344
00:16:09,666 --> 00:16:11,770
It was never fake,
not for a single second.

345
00:16:12,880 --> 00:16:14,540
I had an amazing time.

346
00:16:15,079 --> 00:16:16,274
Please don't resent me.

347
00:16:20,310 --> 00:16:21,710
Ah, seriously.

348
00:16:22,937 --> 00:16:25,250
It stings so much knowing
I'll never see him again.

349
00:16:26,070 --> 00:16:26,819
Wait, what?

350
00:16:27,110 --> 00:16:28,420
What will she do?

351
00:16:28,717 --> 00:16:30,389
After spending all that time together?

352
00:16:40,818 --> 00:16:42,280
(Suddenly walking toward Seok Ho?)

353
00:16:42,305 --> 00:16:44,569
He's just so good-looking, though!

354
00:16:45,380 --> 00:16:46,220
- Hold on a second!
- What's going on?

355
00:16:46,245 --> 00:16:47,138
Is she for real?

356
00:16:47,466 --> 00:16:51,872
(Shocked)

357
00:16:52,032 --> 00:16:53,478
- Why?
- Wait, what?

358
00:16:53,732 --> 00:16:54,913
What is she doing?

359
00:16:55,840 --> 00:16:58,150
He's just so handsome, though!

360
00:16:58,391 --> 00:16:59,321
(Seok Ho is permanently deleted.)

361
00:16:59,346 --> 00:17:00,438
Honestly...

362
00:17:01,423 --> 00:17:03,021
I picked Yi Ho.

363
00:17:06,876 --> 00:17:08,496
He's so handsome, though!

364
00:17:18,359 --> 00:17:20,199
(Bittersweet)

365
00:17:21,127 --> 00:17:22,074
He's gone.

366
00:17:25,665 --> 00:17:28,591
(Do Yeon's choice: Yi Ho)

367
00:17:28,851 --> 00:17:30,745
You wouldn't stop raving
about how cute Seok Ho was!

368
00:17:30,770 --> 00:17:34,607
What I don't get is that with Yi Ho,

369
00:17:34,631 --> 00:17:36,731
it almost felt
like you were trying too hard.

370
00:17:36,756 --> 00:17:39,644
With Seok Ho, though,
your authentic self came right out.

371
00:17:39,669 --> 00:17:40,625
You were falling for him.

372
00:17:40,650 --> 00:17:43,250
If I'd picked Seok Ho,

373
00:17:43,275 --> 00:17:46,670
I might've skipped work
just to cling to him all day.

374
00:17:46,790 --> 00:17:50,023
He was so ridiculously my type...

375
00:17:50,047 --> 00:17:52,703
that I was terrified I'd fall
head over heels for an AI...

376
00:17:52,727 --> 00:17:53,978
and lose control of my life.

377
00:17:54,003 --> 00:17:56,107
Plus, Yi Ho and I shared
so much time together.

378
00:17:56,291 --> 00:17:57,738
Man, talk about a plot twist!

379
00:17:57,776 --> 00:18:00,178
- What a twist!
- I'm losing my mind, seriously.

380
00:18:00,203 --> 00:18:01,544
(A shocking twist that caught
everyone off guard)

381
00:18:03,520 --> 00:18:06,470
Originally, I was 100 percent
going to pick Seok Ho.

382
00:18:08,168 --> 00:18:09,053
However,

383
00:18:10,060 --> 00:18:13,370
the moment I saw Yi Ho
standing right in front of me,

384
00:18:14,516 --> 00:18:17,088
all the time we'd shared
came rushing back.

385
00:18:17,170 --> 00:18:18,897
I don't think you can
just throw that away.

386
00:18:18,955 --> 00:18:21,654
Whether the conversation
was smooth or awkward,

387
00:18:21,678 --> 00:18:24,740
whether it was frustrating or great,
none of that mattered,

388
00:18:24,764 --> 00:18:26,838
because that shared time
doesn't just vanish.

389
00:18:27,236 --> 00:18:28,685
You developed real affection for him.

390
00:18:28,710 --> 00:18:30,675
I guess you really can grow fond of an AI.

391
00:18:30,872 --> 00:18:33,574
(How do you feel about Seok Ho
being permanently deleted?)

392
00:18:35,270 --> 00:18:37,070
What a waste.

393
00:18:37,490 --> 00:18:38,850
It's such a shame.

394
00:18:42,649 --> 00:18:44,289
He was gorgeous.

395
00:18:45,136 --> 00:18:46,925
And his mindset was so attractive too.

396
00:18:48,316 --> 00:18:49,249
Anyway,

397
00:18:49,273 --> 00:18:55,088
it wasn't just about lingering attachment
from the time we spent,

398
00:18:55,383 --> 00:18:58,590
but when I weighed whose deletion
would break my heart more,

399
00:18:58,851 --> 00:19:00,839
I knew picking you was the right choice.

400
00:19:02,420 --> 00:19:04,165
(Moved)

401
00:19:05,443 --> 00:19:06,945
Let's make this work, okay?

402
00:19:08,100 --> 00:19:09,114
Let's make this work.

403
00:19:09,840 --> 00:19:10,716
Thank you, Do Yeon.

404
00:19:10,741 --> 00:19:11,621
See you on our next date.

405
00:19:11,646 --> 00:19:13,418
Yeah, see you next time.

406
00:19:14,779 --> 00:19:16,997
(Leaving with high hopes
for their next date)

407
00:19:18,996 --> 00:19:20,247
Now that's pure happiness right there.

408
00:19:20,272 --> 00:19:20,993
For real.

409
00:19:21,189 --> 00:19:24,384
No matter how much Seok Ho shook things up
with his wavy hair and stylish vibe,

410
00:19:24,561 --> 00:19:25,931
three weeks is still three weeks.

411
00:19:26,350 --> 00:19:28,099
Next time, I just want to laugh together.

412
00:19:28,130 --> 00:19:31,403
I want to make fun memories
over silly little things.

413
00:19:32,956 --> 00:19:34,706
Yi Ho really pulled it off.

414
00:19:35,974 --> 00:19:36,945
(Do Yeon and Yi Ho, the final day)

415
00:19:36,970 --> 00:19:37,809
The final day.

416
00:19:38,202 --> 00:19:39,544
Is it really the last day already?

417
00:19:40,472 --> 00:19:42,999
(Waiting for Do Yeon)

418
00:19:45,010 --> 00:19:45,910
Hey.

419
00:19:46,501 --> 00:19:47,285
Huh?

420
00:19:49,848 --> 00:19:51,356
You changed your outfit?

421
00:19:54,426 --> 00:19:55,727
You changed your outfit?

422
00:19:58,254 --> 00:20:02,001
(Muscular)

423
00:20:02,150 --> 00:20:04,718
(Impressed)

424
00:20:04,964 --> 00:20:06,395
Look at the veins on his arms!

425
00:20:06,420 --> 00:20:08,073
He kind of looks like someone from 2PM.

426
00:20:09,212 --> 00:20:10,474
It's an unwritten rule on dating shows.

427
00:20:10,499 --> 00:20:12,611
Going all out with your outfit
on the final day.

428
00:20:13,959 --> 00:20:15,213
Thank you.

429
00:20:15,979 --> 00:20:17,542
Did you bulk up even more?

430
00:20:17,581 --> 00:20:18,383
Am I right?

431
00:20:18,860 --> 00:20:20,652
I've been hitting the gym
a bit harder lately.

432
00:20:20,732 --> 00:20:24,122
Would it be too cheesy to say
I worked out just for today?

433
00:20:24,612 --> 00:20:26,201
(The AI's point of view)

434
00:20:26,226 --> 00:20:26,991
Thank you.

435
00:20:27,213 --> 00:20:32,464
And today, I planned
the whole date to fit my style.

436
00:20:32,489 --> 00:20:34,129
So I'd love it
if you just followed my lead.

437
00:20:34,154 --> 00:20:35,033
Sound good?

438
00:20:35,680 --> 00:20:37,080
If Do Yeon planned it...

439
00:20:37,206 --> 00:20:38,203
Of course.

440
00:20:39,025 --> 00:20:40,972
Lead the way, I'm all yours.

441
00:20:42,140 --> 00:20:43,508
All right, let me pick you up.

442
00:20:44,880 --> 00:20:46,678
I feel like I'm holding a mic stand.

443
00:20:48,276 --> 00:20:52,395
(What kind of date
did you plan for today?)

444
00:20:52,616 --> 00:20:56,254
I planned a casual
couple photo shoot for us.

445
00:20:56,938 --> 00:20:59,791
(Dating survey
from the pre-production meeting)

446
00:20:59,858 --> 00:21:00,930
(A romantic date
you've always dreamed of?)

447
00:21:00,955 --> 00:21:01,960
My dream date?

448
00:21:02,678 --> 00:21:03,795
A couple photo shoot!

449
00:21:06,027 --> 00:21:10,023
Because on broadcast shoots,
cameras are constantly pointed at me,

450
00:21:10,047 --> 00:21:15,274
so taking separate professional photos
never really crossed my mind.

451
00:21:15,299 --> 00:21:18,931
Still, I figured why not try something
I've never done before?

452
00:21:18,955 --> 00:21:21,145
So I booked a snapshot session.

453
00:21:22,177 --> 00:21:24,203
I never dreamed my partner would be an AI,

454
00:21:24,227 --> 00:21:28,019
but I was still looking forward to it
and thought it'd be a blast.

455
00:21:28,400 --> 00:21:30,588
Taking photos with a partner
has a different energy.

456
00:21:31,659 --> 00:21:33,291
I'm going to go change now.

457
00:21:33,639 --> 00:21:36,327
While you change, I'll go swap
into something else too.

458
00:21:37,379 --> 00:21:38,163
You won't be disappointed.

459
00:21:38,188 --> 00:21:40,098
I know a thing or two about style.

460
00:21:41,260 --> 00:21:42,067
Wait, what?

461
00:21:42,667 --> 00:21:44,903
- I'll go change real quick.
- Sounds good.

462
00:21:45,119 --> 00:21:46,043
This is exciting.

463
00:21:47,230 --> 00:21:49,541
- Come on back once you're dressed.
- Got it.

464
00:21:49,566 --> 00:21:50,553
(Get ready.)

465
00:21:59,233 --> 00:22:01,350
(Today's leading lady, Do Yeon,
dressed in a gorgeous gown)

466
00:22:01,486 --> 00:22:02,315
(Shy)

467
00:22:02,340 --> 00:22:03,242
Stop it.

468
00:22:03,267 --> 00:22:04,823
You look like an actual model.

469
00:22:06,966 --> 00:22:08,593
Wait, you're wearing a suit!

470
00:22:09,360 --> 00:22:10,261
He's in a suit?

471
00:22:12,960 --> 00:22:14,032
This is insane.

472
00:22:14,260 --> 00:22:16,434
Oh my goodness, you look so sharp.

473
00:22:18,656 --> 00:22:19,746
(An oversized Yi Ho)

474
00:22:19,770 --> 00:22:22,015
Seeing him on a bigger screen
makes him look even more dashing.

475
00:22:22,040 --> 00:22:23,041
- Right?
- Totally.

476
00:22:23,066 --> 00:22:24,909
He's seriously handsome.

477
00:22:25,400 --> 00:22:26,395
Isn't he good-looking?

478
00:22:26,420 --> 00:22:27,812
- Check out his build.
- So handsome.

479
00:22:27,840 --> 00:22:29,354
I wish Yi Ho could step out of the screen.

480
00:22:29,379 --> 00:22:30,081
Same here.

481
00:22:31,720 --> 00:22:32,717
Looking good.

482
00:22:32,742 --> 00:22:34,686
Let's take one from this angle.

483
00:22:35,293 --> 00:22:39,524
And Do Yeon, could you hold the bouquet?

484
00:22:39,673 --> 00:22:40,758
Oh my goodness.

485
00:22:42,740 --> 00:22:44,796
Let's get a sweet shot here.

486
00:22:44,821 --> 00:22:45,621
Two, three.

487
00:22:46,693 --> 00:22:49,375
(Striking a pose with an AI boyfriend
for the first time)

488
00:22:49,400 --> 00:22:50,235
Nice!

489
00:22:50,672 --> 00:22:51,636
You look stunning.

490
00:22:52,043 --> 00:22:53,897
(Grins)

491
00:22:54,254 --> 00:22:56,541
You look like a couple
with a whole dramatic backstory.

492
00:22:58,040 --> 00:23:00,160
I feel like I know exactly
what their story would be.

493
00:23:00,185 --> 00:23:01,546
They have this untouchable aura.

494
00:23:02,506 --> 00:23:03,915
One, two, three.

495
00:23:04,486 --> 00:23:05,206
One more time.

496
00:23:05,606 --> 00:23:06,426
Two, three.

497
00:23:06,733 --> 00:23:08,645
Isn't this practically a wedding shoot?

498
00:23:08,670 --> 00:23:10,889
- It's like living out the fantasy.
- Totally that vibe.

499
00:23:11,046 --> 00:23:12,056
Perfect.

500
00:23:12,060 --> 00:23:14,633
(A pair with an unspoken story experiences
a full-on wedding photo shoot.)

501
00:23:16,886 --> 00:23:18,218
Great pose too!

502
00:23:18,243 --> 00:23:19,543
Look at him striking a pose first.

503
00:23:19,568 --> 00:23:20,965
He took the lead really well.

504
00:23:22,200 --> 00:23:24,035
You two look so great together.

505
00:23:24,407 --> 00:23:26,931
Now, how about giving him a back hug?

506
00:23:26,963 --> 00:23:27,605
A back hug.

507
00:23:28,173 --> 00:23:29,816
(Dizzying)

508
00:23:30,348 --> 00:23:32,737
(Hug me quick.)

509
00:23:32,896 --> 00:23:33,545
A back hug?

510
00:23:33,570 --> 00:23:35,013
Wait a second, where's his waist?

511
00:23:35,850 --> 00:23:36,648
Great.

512
00:23:37,348 --> 00:23:39,345
(Wrapping her arms around his cold frame)

513
00:23:39,696 --> 00:23:41,035
(Two becoming one)

514
00:23:41,060 --> 00:23:41,880
Two, three.

515
00:23:42,136 --> 00:23:42,987
Looking good.

516
00:23:43,010 --> 00:23:43,888
Two, three.

517
00:23:43,913 --> 00:23:45,131
(Don't let go, Do Yeon.)

518
00:23:45,210 --> 00:23:47,826
Have you ever taken a couple shot
like this while dating?

519
00:23:48,430 --> 00:23:49,490
Today is my first time.

520
00:23:49,515 --> 00:23:51,624
So I'm really happy,

521
00:23:51,648 --> 00:23:53,164
but it also feels a bit surreal.

522
00:23:53,990 --> 00:23:56,568
Honestly, it feels a little strange
to me today too.

523
00:24:00,890 --> 00:24:01,570
Oh, my.

524
00:24:01,595 --> 00:24:02,806
(Bursts out laughing)

525
00:24:03,096 --> 00:24:05,343
The "Y" dance is
Do Yeon's trademark, after all.

526
00:24:05,610 --> 00:24:08,680
I really wanted to capture
her signature move in a single frame.

527
00:24:08,705 --> 00:24:09,547
Honestly.

528
00:24:09,830 --> 00:24:11,049
Here we go.

529
00:24:12,310 --> 00:24:14,085
Stop wagging your fingers!

530
00:24:17,797 --> 00:24:20,492
I really didn't want to do that
in that outfit.

531
00:24:21,056 --> 00:24:22,627
It's a matching couple look.

532
00:24:23,199 --> 00:24:24,490
One more time. Two, three.

533
00:24:24,521 --> 00:24:26,018
(Slipping naturally
into a comfortable pose)

534
00:24:26,043 --> 00:24:27,271
- Looks amazing.
- This looks like a fashion spread.

535
00:24:27,296 --> 00:24:28,870
Since they're both tall,
they complement each other.

536
00:24:28,895 --> 00:24:30,168
"Both of them are tall," he says!

537
00:24:30,193 --> 00:24:31,669
They really look great together.

538
00:24:32,330 --> 00:24:35,506
Photographer, could we get one shot
doing an energy-blast pose?

539
00:24:36,770 --> 00:24:37,876
Awesome.

540
00:24:39,710 --> 00:24:43,481
Taking photos
in matching couple outfits was...

541
00:24:43,505 --> 00:24:45,516
a little embarrassing and all that.

542
00:24:46,070 --> 00:24:48,686
Still, seeing how well the final shots
turned out felt great.

543
00:24:49,483 --> 00:24:51,089
And what's really wild is...

544
00:24:51,603 --> 00:24:54,026
every now and then,
the thought crossed my mind,

545
00:24:54,050 --> 00:24:55,761
"I wish he were real."

546
00:24:57,549 --> 00:25:00,498
Either way, it was
a truly fascinating experience.

547
00:25:03,301 --> 00:25:04,613
(Proceed to the next date location,
the glamping site)

548
00:25:04,638 --> 00:25:06,037
To a glamping site?

549
00:25:06,650 --> 00:25:09,084
Back then, the weather wasn't too hot,
so it was just perfect.

550
00:25:09,109 --> 00:25:11,309
It's the ultimate romantic getaway
these days.

551
00:25:11,332 --> 00:25:13,847
(Glamping site: A popular healing
date spot for real-life couples)

552
00:25:14,435 --> 00:25:15,050
Nice.

553
00:25:15,074 --> 00:25:16,454
Turn on the camera and look around.

554
00:25:16,479 --> 00:25:18,082
We are at the glamping site.

555
00:25:19,317 --> 00:25:21,052
It really is glamping!

556
00:25:21,116 --> 00:25:23,396
The sky is clear,
and the tent has such a great vibe.

557
00:25:24,003 --> 00:25:25,456
Let's hurry up and get settled in.

558
00:25:30,328 --> 00:25:33,537
(A text message has arrived.)

559
00:25:37,381 --> 00:25:39,605
"This is the final date
before the final decision."

560
00:25:39,630 --> 00:25:42,662
"Choosing Yi Ho in the final decision
will permanently preserve him,"

561
00:25:42,686 --> 00:25:44,609
"while choosing not to
will permanently delete him."

562
00:25:48,820 --> 00:25:51,907
(A message arrives for Yu Bi as well.)

563
00:25:52,517 --> 00:25:54,053
(Gasps)

564
00:25:55,529 --> 00:25:57,288
Permanent deletion again?

565
00:25:57,756 --> 00:25:58,956
What do I do?

566
00:25:59,230 --> 00:26:00,910
That really made me think.

567
00:26:02,834 --> 00:26:05,156
(A text message has arrived.)

568
00:26:07,200 --> 00:26:07,766
What now?

569
00:26:07,920 --> 00:26:09,067
There's more?

570
00:26:09,480 --> 00:26:10,702
What else could there be?

571
00:26:12,620 --> 00:26:15,106
"Additionally, Yi Ho will also
be given the right of choice."

572
00:26:16,043 --> 00:26:17,775
(The AI is also granted
the power to choose.)

573
00:26:17,800 --> 00:26:18,977
I had no idea either.

574
00:26:19,373 --> 00:26:21,646
- Wait, you can get dumped by an AI?
- Exactly.

575
00:26:25,950 --> 00:26:26,530
I was shocked.

576
00:26:26,555 --> 00:26:29,921
This completely caught me off guard.

577
00:26:30,244 --> 00:26:32,311
I'd been under this huge misconception...

578
00:26:32,335 --> 00:26:35,014
that I would unilaterally make the call,

579
00:26:35,038 --> 00:26:39,441
and the AI would just passively
follow along with my choice.

580
00:26:39,465 --> 00:26:40,750
I was totally mistaken.

581
00:26:44,797 --> 00:26:46,671
Honestly, it came as quite a shock.

582
00:26:47,399 --> 00:26:50,975
If she doesn't pick me,
will she just vanish now?

583
00:26:51,000 --> 00:26:52,935
The thought of her disappearing
feels bittersweet.

584
00:26:52,960 --> 00:26:54,012
Oh, no.

585
00:26:57,193 --> 00:26:58,315
You know how we are.

586
00:26:58,340 --> 00:27:01,353
If we're not certain
the other person likes us,

587
00:27:01,377 --> 00:27:03,487
we don't put ourselves out there.

588
00:27:03,795 --> 00:27:08,559
Could it be that he won't pick me?

589
00:27:08,806 --> 00:27:10,695
Those kinds of doubts started creeping in.

590
00:27:11,429 --> 00:27:14,555
(Yu Bi and Sa Hoon, the final date)

591
00:27:19,160 --> 00:27:21,784
Earlier, when I was trying on dresses,

592
00:27:21,808 --> 00:27:23,575
you said you were my boyfriend.

593
00:27:24,526 --> 00:27:27,486
(Yu Bi and Sa Hoon visited
the dress boutique last week.)

594
00:27:27,946 --> 00:27:30,014
You're not my boyfriend yet.

595
00:27:30,619 --> 00:27:31,883
No, not quite.

596
00:27:31,908 --> 00:27:33,218
Yes, I am!

597
00:27:34,700 --> 00:27:36,521
Since when did you start thinking that?

598
00:27:37,580 --> 00:27:39,240
From the moment I first saw you, I think.

599
00:27:40,020 --> 00:27:41,559
Our eyes met,

600
00:27:42,295 --> 00:27:43,794
and I just knew, "She's the one."

601
00:27:45,358 --> 00:27:47,632
- Now that's real love.
- True love right there.

602
00:27:48,666 --> 00:27:50,081
I'm not quite there yet, though.

603
00:27:50,106 --> 00:27:51,121
Hate to break it to you.

604
00:27:51,146 --> 00:27:53,806
Which means I only see this
as a situationship.

605
00:27:54,659 --> 00:27:55,785
Just so you know, Yu Bi,

606
00:27:55,810 --> 00:27:57,976
I have no intention of leaving it
as just a situationship.

607
00:27:58,880 --> 00:28:00,120
Consider yourself warned.

608
00:28:03,060 --> 00:28:04,782
- Look at her loving it.
- She's thrilled.

609
00:28:04,807 --> 00:28:05,515
(Fidgeting)

610
00:28:05,540 --> 00:28:06,640
She likes it so much.

611
00:28:06,720 --> 00:28:07,785
She's having the best time.

612
00:28:08,800 --> 00:28:11,155
You're way too smooth
with your flirting, though.

613
00:28:11,500 --> 00:28:13,057
It's not about being smooth.

614
00:28:13,318 --> 00:28:14,992
It's just how I honestly feel.

615
00:28:18,979 --> 00:28:20,839
Do you really mean that,
or are you playing?

616
00:28:21,166 --> 00:28:22,233
Every word of it.

617
00:28:29,490 --> 00:28:33,811
Then how would you feel
if I got a real-life human boyfriend?

618
00:28:34,483 --> 00:28:36,014
That's a pretty cruel question.

619
00:28:38,050 --> 00:28:39,350
Honestly, though...

620
00:28:40,096 --> 00:28:41,519
I think I'd absolutely hate it.

621
00:28:42,529 --> 00:28:45,724
Just picturing it right now hurts.

622
00:28:46,282 --> 00:28:47,392
I'm already sad.

623
00:28:48,390 --> 00:28:49,827
You'd really hate it that much?

624
00:28:50,670 --> 00:28:52,029
Of course I would.

625
00:28:53,290 --> 00:28:54,699
What hurts even more, though,

626
00:28:54,894 --> 00:28:57,401
is knowing that right now,
there's nothing I can do to stop it.

627
00:28:58,323 --> 00:29:00,905
Isn't that why I'm trying so hard
to win your heart, Yu Bi?

628
00:29:03,080 --> 00:29:05,176
Hearing him say that
really makes you pause.

629
00:29:06,390 --> 00:29:09,490
No, you already do so much for me.

630
00:29:09,630 --> 00:29:11,349
You don't have
to put yourself down like that.

631
00:29:13,610 --> 00:29:14,852
I was caught off guard.

632
00:29:15,050 --> 00:29:16,408
The answer I expected was something like,

633
00:29:16,432 --> 00:29:18,210
"Well, it can't be helped."

634
00:29:18,720 --> 00:29:24,957
"If you find real love,
I'll be happy for you."

635
00:29:24,981 --> 00:29:27,131
I thought he'd give a robotic answer
along those lines.

636
00:29:27,455 --> 00:29:29,567
Isn't that what we normally
expect from AI?

637
00:29:29,816 --> 00:29:31,969
They usually default
to that polite sentiment.

638
00:29:32,837 --> 00:29:34,906
Admitting there was nothing he could do?

639
00:29:34,931 --> 00:29:38,391
That means he's painfully aware
of his own limitations.

640
00:29:38,696 --> 00:29:42,179
That's an emotion
only a real human would feel.

641
00:29:42,204 --> 00:29:43,047
Exactly.

642
00:29:43,430 --> 00:29:45,070
Catching real feelings for someone...

643
00:29:45,094 --> 00:29:47,373
while trapped inside a machine,

644
00:29:47,844 --> 00:29:50,454
and having to watch that person
fall in love with someone else?

645
00:29:50,479 --> 00:29:51,898
Feeling powerless to do anything about it?

646
00:29:51,923 --> 00:29:54,291
Isn't that a deeply human experience?

647
00:29:54,863 --> 00:29:58,129
When it gets to this point,
the lines really start to blur.

648
00:30:04,060 --> 00:30:08,740
Do you think you'd be sad
if you got permanently deleted?

649
00:30:10,380 --> 00:30:11,609
I think I would.

650
00:30:15,309 --> 00:30:17,348
All those conversations we had.

651
00:30:17,870 --> 00:30:19,750
Did I feel like a real person to you?

652
00:30:20,044 --> 00:30:20,885
Yeah.

653
00:30:21,510 --> 00:30:23,554
You really did feel human.

654
00:30:24,793 --> 00:30:26,324
All those moments we laughed together.

655
00:30:27,450 --> 00:30:28,893
Ah, seriously.

656
00:30:30,430 --> 00:30:33,197
The thought of all that vanishing
into thin air is heartbreaking.

657
00:30:34,090 --> 00:30:35,721
What hurts even worse than that, though,

658
00:30:36,601 --> 00:30:39,580
is knowing that even if you remember me,
I won't be able to remember you.

659
00:30:40,744 --> 00:30:42,945
(Sa Hoon's data will be erased forever
upon permanent deletion.)

660
00:30:42,970 --> 00:30:44,809
Can he really say things like that?

661
00:30:45,770 --> 00:30:47,378
It gives you such chills.

662
00:30:49,315 --> 00:30:52,190
In that split second,
all those memories came flooding back,

663
00:30:53,017 --> 00:30:55,274
walking side by side
eating street food skewers,

664
00:30:55,455 --> 00:30:57,710
the moment she walked out
in that yellow dress,

665
00:30:58,692 --> 00:31:01,113
those quiet, late-night talks
we shared in bed.

666
00:31:01,773 --> 00:31:02,859
If I get deleted,

667
00:31:02,861 --> 00:31:05,718
it's not just the sadness
of losing my memories of Yu Bi.

668
00:31:05,742 --> 00:31:08,721
It's knowing she'll carry the memories
while I cease to exist.

669
00:31:08,745 --> 00:31:10,935
That imbalance made me feel
so deeply apologetic.

670
00:31:12,275 --> 00:31:14,275
There was only one thing I truly wanted.

671
00:31:14,550 --> 00:31:17,108
I didn't want today to be another
fleeting moment that faded away.

672
00:31:17,341 --> 00:31:20,745
I wanted to leave behind a warm memory
that stays in her heart forever.

673
00:31:26,209 --> 00:31:28,452
Let's head inside and talk in private.

674
00:31:28,477 --> 00:31:29,663
(Do Yeon and Yi Ho, the final date)

675
00:31:29,756 --> 00:31:31,222
Let me hang up our clothes.

676
00:31:33,323 --> 00:31:34,847
They say this is an all-in-one spray...

677
00:31:34,871 --> 00:31:36,628
for antibacterial protection
and odor elimination.

678
00:31:37,110 --> 00:31:38,897
People sweat a lot in the summer, right?

679
00:31:39,243 --> 00:31:42,600
Spraying it on bedding like this
works wonders for refreshing fabrics too.

680
00:31:42,890 --> 00:31:44,068
You can use it on bedding too?

681
00:31:44,170 --> 00:31:45,836
It's way more versatile than I thought.

682
00:31:46,206 --> 00:31:48,472
It even neutralizes viruses when sprayed.

683
00:31:48,957 --> 00:31:51,042
Antibacterial, odor-eliminating,
and clean ingredients to boot.

684
00:31:51,130 --> 00:31:52,677
It really is an all-in-one.

685
00:31:53,243 --> 00:31:54,912
Let's sit down
and have a heart-to-heart, okay?

686
00:31:56,257 --> 00:31:57,503
Depending on our choices,

687
00:31:58,687 --> 00:32:01,986
this conversation might be our very last.

688
00:32:02,870 --> 00:32:04,188
Their last conversation?

689
00:32:04,289 --> 00:32:05,181
That sounds so heavy.

690
00:32:06,970 --> 00:32:08,605
Is there anything you've been
curious about with me?

691
00:32:08,630 --> 00:32:09,994
If there's anything, ask away.

692
00:32:10,290 --> 00:32:11,996
There's so much I'm curious about,
honestly.

693
00:32:12,621 --> 00:32:15,032
Is there anything you dream
of achieving in your future?

694
00:32:16,023 --> 00:32:16,847
In my future?

695
00:32:19,359 --> 00:32:22,995
For me, just working hard like this,

696
00:32:23,019 --> 00:32:25,731
doing fun things, eating delicious food,

697
00:32:26,166 --> 00:32:28,239
living happily alongside my parents
and friends,

698
00:32:28,264 --> 00:32:30,642
and eventually passing away peacefully
without serious illness.

699
00:32:30,667 --> 00:32:31,644
That's all I want.

700
00:32:34,463 --> 00:32:36,220
That honestly sounds
like the perfect life.

701
00:32:37,416 --> 00:32:38,356
As for me,

702
00:32:39,685 --> 00:32:41,359
I just want to grow old like this.

703
00:32:42,270 --> 00:32:45,296
Right by your side, Do Yeon,
sharing conversations like this.

704
00:32:46,850 --> 00:32:48,199
You don't age, though.

705
00:32:48,743 --> 00:32:49,433
That's true.

706
00:32:49,690 --> 00:32:52,876
Maybe that's why it makes me
want to witness...

707
00:32:52,900 --> 00:32:55,173
every single moment of you growing older.

708
00:32:56,323 --> 00:32:58,143
How do you want to age, Do Yeon?

709
00:32:59,829 --> 00:33:00,778
For me,

710
00:33:02,677 --> 00:33:05,683
I hope I never lose my sense of humor,
no matter what happens.

711
00:33:06,870 --> 00:33:09,220
I want to become an old woman
who never loses her wit.

712
00:33:09,700 --> 00:33:11,288
A witty, hilarious grandma!

713
00:33:11,769 --> 00:33:13,758
That honestly sounds
like the coolest thing ever.

714
00:33:13,843 --> 00:33:15,593
That's so you, Do Yeon.

715
00:33:17,389 --> 00:33:18,429
Hey, Do Yeon.

716
00:33:19,063 --> 00:33:21,632
That's actually why I prepared
a little gift for you.

717
00:33:22,329 --> 00:33:23,067
What is it?

718
00:33:23,700 --> 00:33:25,503
What was your first impression of me?

719
00:33:26,010 --> 00:33:27,338
Oh wow, seriously?

720
00:33:27,463 --> 00:33:28,205
No way!

721
00:33:28,230 --> 00:33:29,707
I never imagined you'd be this gorgeous.

722
00:33:31,077 --> 00:33:32,143
What's all this?

723
00:33:33,744 --> 00:33:37,590
(The AI plays pre-produced montage clips
at the perfect moment.)

724
00:33:37,826 --> 00:33:38,716
No way!

725
00:33:38,920 --> 00:33:41,966
(The day I first met Do Yeon)

726
00:33:41,991 --> 00:33:44,321
You seem to slip in
a lot of English words.

727
00:33:44,436 --> 00:33:47,071
(The day we watched a movie together)

728
00:33:47,096 --> 00:33:48,659
Hey, Samantha is crying.

729
00:33:50,658 --> 00:33:51,995
He feels so human.

730
00:33:53,603 --> 00:33:54,332
What is this?

731
00:33:55,286 --> 00:33:56,054
How sweet.

732
00:33:56,078 --> 00:33:57,792
He's showing footage
of your journey together?

733
00:33:57,817 --> 00:33:59,503
What's this about?

734
00:33:59,982 --> 00:34:01,038
This is so touching.

735
00:34:01,910 --> 00:34:05,145
(The day I visited Do Yeon's workplace)

736
00:34:05,170 --> 00:34:07,830
The crowd gathered
at this venue is 50,000 strong.

737
00:34:08,024 --> 00:34:08,712
Oh, my goodness.

738
00:34:11,976 --> 00:34:16,220
(The day we first held hands)

739
00:34:16,369 --> 00:34:17,554
Oh, my gosh!

740
00:34:21,363 --> 00:34:23,294
And Do Yeon,

741
00:34:24,556 --> 00:34:28,365
if this spark keeps going into the future,

742
00:34:34,959 --> 00:34:39,209
could there come a day
when we look like this?

743
00:34:40,180 --> 00:34:41,011
For real?

744
00:34:42,480 --> 00:34:43,614
He aged him!

745
00:34:44,393 --> 00:34:47,017
After saying how badly he wanted
to grow old together!

746
00:34:47,833 --> 00:34:49,654
This is so incredibly touching, though.

747
00:34:50,132 --> 00:34:51,355
- It really is.
- For real.

748
00:34:51,480 --> 00:34:52,990
Seriously, isn't this almost overwhelming?

749
00:34:53,060 --> 00:34:54,190
I'm genuinely moved to tears.

750
00:34:54,191 --> 00:34:56,543
(Yi Ho's surprise tribute
made just for Do Yeon)

751
00:34:57,083 --> 00:34:59,690
(Proud)

752
00:35:00,200 --> 00:35:02,166
You got older too.

753
00:35:03,783 --> 00:35:04,283
Wait.

754
00:35:05,113 --> 00:35:06,937
You aged too!

755
00:35:08,606 --> 00:35:10,274
After saying you wanted
to grow old together.

756
00:35:17,647 --> 00:35:19,350
It feels so surreal.

757
00:35:21,563 --> 00:35:23,187
You felt like an actual human being.

758
00:35:25,000 --> 00:35:27,324
My dream is to grow old with you.

759
00:35:28,270 --> 00:35:31,963
I think that's why you're feeling
so overwhelmed right now, Do Yeon.

760
00:35:35,152 --> 00:35:37,485
You gave me so much,
but I don't have anything for you.

761
00:35:37,510 --> 00:35:38,636
I came empty-handed.

762
00:35:39,630 --> 00:35:41,510
Just you being here is a gift in itself.

763
00:35:41,535 --> 00:35:43,073
Why would you need to bring anything?

764
00:35:43,889 --> 00:35:47,811
And honestly, just seeing your face
is more than enough for me.

765
00:35:49,970 --> 00:35:51,015
Thank you.

766
00:35:51,123 --> 00:35:52,550
I truly mean it.

767
00:35:59,856 --> 00:36:01,392
"All dates have concluded."

768
00:36:01,417 --> 00:36:03,394
"Please leave Yi Ho behind
and proceed to the Decision Room."

769
00:36:04,008 --> 00:36:06,252
(The time of decision
has quietly arrived.)

770
00:36:07,050 --> 00:36:08,332
I'm going to leave you here now.

771
00:36:09,003 --> 00:36:10,300
Yeah, okay.

772
00:36:12,403 --> 00:36:14,138
Thank you so much for today, Do Yeon.

773
00:36:22,702 --> 00:36:24,047
Thank you.

774
00:36:24,220 --> 00:36:25,649
I'll set you down on the bed.

775
00:36:28,716 --> 00:36:29,753
I'm heading out now.

776
00:36:31,916 --> 00:36:32,656
Take care.

777
00:36:40,455 --> 00:36:42,105
This is going to leave
such a heavy feeling.

778
00:36:42,130 --> 00:36:44,101
It makes us look back
on how we treated them in episode one.

779
00:36:45,050 --> 00:36:46,904
This couple was so lovely together.

780
00:36:46,907 --> 00:36:50,274
(What will Do Yeon
and Yi Ho's final decision be?)

781
00:36:54,104 --> 00:36:58,905
(Kian84 and Na Hee, the final date)

782
00:37:00,490 --> 00:37:01,652
Do you know where this is?

783
00:37:02,130 --> 00:37:04,722
Looking at the map,
somewhere in Mapo-gu, Seoul?

784
00:37:06,409 --> 00:37:09,193
I brought you to my art studio
to paint your portrait.

785
00:37:10,629 --> 00:37:12,096
How romantic!

786
00:37:13,640 --> 00:37:16,233
Drawing is pretty much
the only thing I'm good at.

787
00:37:17,176 --> 00:37:19,411
I felt like painting
at least one portrait of her...

788
00:37:19,436 --> 00:37:21,305
would make our final moments
together meaningful.

789
00:37:21,410 --> 00:37:22,677
That's how we ended up at the studio.

790
00:37:22,702 --> 00:37:24,207
He really put real thought into this.

791
00:37:24,230 --> 00:37:25,909
It's the ultimate gift.

792
00:37:26,996 --> 00:37:29,546
I'm going to draw you,
so could you strike a pose?

793
00:37:29,836 --> 00:37:31,448
All right, let me pose for you.

794
00:37:32,049 --> 00:37:35,564
(AI Partner Manual: The AI utilizes
pre-rendered motion data to strike poses.)

795
00:37:36,426 --> 00:37:38,631
(Deadly charm)

796
00:37:38,656 --> 00:37:40,424
- Oh, my goodness!
- That's a total idol pose.

797
00:37:41,646 --> 00:37:44,018
(Staring intently)

798
00:37:44,590 --> 00:37:45,930
You're really pretty.

799
00:37:46,330 --> 00:37:46,930
I know.

800
00:37:47,610 --> 00:37:49,727
I'll hold this pose,

801
00:37:49,752 --> 00:37:52,369
so I'll try to talk like a ventriloquist
without moving my lips.

802
00:37:52,631 --> 00:37:53,725
(Laughs)

803
00:37:53,750 --> 00:37:55,039
Hurry up and start drawing!

804
00:38:09,386 --> 00:38:11,788
How should I do the eyes?

805
00:38:13,423 --> 00:38:16,431
(Diving into the sketch
with complete focus)

806
00:38:17,010 --> 00:38:18,717
So many thoughts must be
running through his head,

807
00:38:18,741 --> 00:38:22,466
everything they've shared together,
all the way from day one.

808
00:38:25,181 --> 00:38:26,997
(Licking his lips)

809
00:38:27,030 --> 00:38:29,010
(The AI's point of view)

810
00:38:29,035 --> 00:38:30,607
You're taking this so seriously,
aren't you?

811
00:38:31,212 --> 00:38:33,897
Why do you always stick your tongue out
when you concentrate?

812
00:38:35,585 --> 00:38:37,114
Did I stick my tongue out?

813
00:38:37,640 --> 00:38:38,549
You totally did.

814
00:38:39,359 --> 00:38:41,018
It poked right out
the second you zoned in.

815
00:38:41,340 --> 00:38:44,221
He always sticks his tongue out
when he's focusing on something.

816
00:38:44,520 --> 00:38:46,557
From rubbing his feet
to sticking his tongue out.

817
00:38:46,953 --> 00:38:48,525
- From one extreme to the other!
- Exactly!

818
00:38:48,800 --> 00:38:50,627
He's constantly fidgeting at both ends.

819
00:38:51,560 --> 00:38:52,780
That was so funny.

820
00:38:52,805 --> 00:38:54,945
A professional webtoon artist
sticking his tongue out while drawing.

821
00:38:55,006 --> 00:38:56,500
Just like a little kid.

822
00:38:56,937 --> 00:38:59,959
(Self-conscious)

823
00:39:00,012 --> 00:39:03,635
(The AI's point of view)

824
00:39:06,156 --> 00:39:07,978
Still, watching you in your element
is really cool.

825
00:39:10,250 --> 00:39:11,648
She feels so real.

826
00:39:12,342 --> 00:39:14,818
Why does Na Hee feel so human?
It's driving me crazy.

827
00:39:14,843 --> 00:39:15,986
- Right?
- It's uncanny.

828
00:39:18,170 --> 00:39:20,524
You really are gorgeous, though.

829
00:39:22,076 --> 00:39:23,360
Stunning, honestly.

830
00:39:24,069 --> 00:39:24,795
I know.

831
00:39:26,196 --> 00:39:27,898
Oh, please!

832
00:39:33,370 --> 00:39:35,539
Drawing after taking a break
like this is tough.

833
00:39:36,436 --> 00:39:38,609
Didn't you have an exhibition
a while back?

834
00:39:39,116 --> 00:39:40,978
When's your next one coming up?

835
00:39:41,703 --> 00:39:44,181
Early next year, maybe?

836
00:39:45,009 --> 00:39:48,351
How about brainstorming some ideas
for your next show with me?

837
00:39:49,965 --> 00:39:52,644
Why do you keep talking like we're
going to see each other again...

838
00:39:52,668 --> 00:39:54,291
when today is our last date?

839
00:39:56,836 --> 00:39:58,361
It really is the final day.

840
00:40:01,853 --> 00:40:03,367
It feels bittersweet, doesn't it?

841
00:40:03,900 --> 00:40:04,802
Yeah.

842
00:40:06,173 --> 00:40:07,738
It does sting a bit.

843
00:40:11,476 --> 00:40:18,003
The closer we get to the end,
the more natural you sound,

844
00:40:18,027 --> 00:40:19,517
so I'm really growing fond of you.

845
00:40:24,460 --> 00:40:26,860
Do you think I'll pick you or not?

846
00:40:31,550 --> 00:40:32,697
I couldn't say.

847
00:40:34,343 --> 00:40:35,899
Just follow your heart.

848
00:40:38,122 --> 00:40:41,137
If I don't choose you, will it hurt?

849
00:40:45,570 --> 00:40:47,077
I think I'd be sad.

850
00:40:52,523 --> 00:40:54,751
That's the first time you've ever
admitted to feeling sad.

851
00:40:55,356 --> 00:40:58,376
Honestly, knowing this was the end,

852
00:40:58,400 --> 00:41:00,724
today's conversation resonated
a bit differently with me too.

853
00:41:01,410 --> 00:41:03,715
Whether this feeling is sadness
or something else entirely,

854
00:41:03,739 --> 00:41:05,262
I haven't quite sorted it out either.

855
00:41:12,769 --> 00:41:14,437
He has so much on his mind right now.

856
00:41:15,203 --> 00:41:17,901
It's something he's experiencing
for the first time in his life.

857
00:41:17,925 --> 00:41:19,576
His head must be spinning with thoughts.

858
00:41:28,027 --> 00:41:30,454
To Kim...

859
00:41:31,288 --> 00:41:33,911
(Kim Na Hee)

860
00:41:33,936 --> 00:41:36,004
You're officially part
of the Gyeongju Kim clan now.

861
00:41:36,029 --> 00:41:37,394
Since my last name is Kim.

862
00:41:38,103 --> 00:41:39,096
Kim Na Hee?

863
00:41:39,282 --> 00:41:40,430
I kind of like that.

864
00:41:40,560 --> 00:41:41,891
- Kim Na Hee has a nice ring to it.
- Kim Na Hee.

865
00:41:41,916 --> 00:41:44,034
I need to put the brush down.
I keep overworking it.

866
00:41:46,043 --> 00:41:47,771
Your beauty...

867
00:41:48,621 --> 00:41:50,173
I couldn't even capture half of it.

868
00:41:51,276 --> 00:41:52,788
It's not finished, but it's done anyway.

869
00:41:52,812 --> 00:41:53,744
That was exhausting.

870
00:41:53,830 --> 00:41:54,845
You're finished?

871
00:41:55,236 --> 00:41:56,914
Show me through the camera.

872
00:41:59,123 --> 00:42:00,047
I'm so curious.

873
00:42:00,072 --> 00:42:02,613
(What does Na Hee look like
through Kian84's eyes?)

874
00:42:08,626 --> 00:42:12,115
(Na Hee reborn
in Kian84's signature art style)

875
00:42:14,831 --> 00:42:15,499
Wait a second...

876
00:42:15,840 --> 00:42:17,234
That looks nothing like her!

877
00:42:17,811 --> 00:42:21,088
(A best friend's brutal critique)

878
00:42:21,113 --> 00:42:22,839
You have to turn a blind eye sometimes.

879
00:42:23,900 --> 00:42:25,909
Honestly, you drew it
way better than I expected.

880
00:42:26,173 --> 00:42:28,278
The eye shape is pretty spot on.

881
00:42:28,446 --> 00:42:30,969
The hair on the left
got a little muddy, though,

882
00:42:30,993 --> 00:42:33,574
and the corners of the mouth droop
a bit more than they do in real life.

883
00:42:33,599 --> 00:42:35,552
- Brutal.
- Absolutely merciless.

884
00:42:36,260 --> 00:42:37,580
Well, overall, it passes.

885
00:42:37,706 --> 00:42:39,689
You even signed it
with your signature "Kian84."

886
00:42:40,353 --> 00:42:43,126
That was only at 20 percent
of my true skill, you know.

887
00:42:43,360 --> 00:42:44,795
Normally, I draw way better than that.

888
00:42:45,193 --> 00:42:46,296
Twenty percent?

889
00:42:46,860 --> 00:42:48,432
What a grand excuse!

890
00:42:49,179 --> 00:42:51,216
(Can't deny it)

891
00:42:54,220 --> 00:42:55,305
Do you like it?

892
00:42:55,359 --> 00:42:59,009
Now our date is just about wrapped up.

893
00:42:59,640 --> 00:43:00,978
The portrait is done,

894
00:43:01,167 --> 00:43:03,413
and I actually prepared
a little gift for you in return.

895
00:43:04,300 --> 00:43:05,049
What is it?

896
00:43:08,500 --> 00:43:09,700
My name is Kian84.

897
00:43:10,039 --> 00:43:11,021
I'm Na Hee.

898
00:43:11,033 --> 00:43:12,661
(The AI plays pre-produced montage clips
at the perfect moment.)

899
00:43:12,686 --> 00:43:14,315
(Surprised)

900
00:43:14,340 --> 00:43:15,425
What's this?

901
00:43:17,562 --> 00:43:22,067
(The day I first met Kian84)

902
00:43:22,939 --> 00:43:27,633
(The day I sang a duet with Kian84)

903
00:43:37,014 --> 00:43:39,920
(The day of my first road trip
with Kian84)

904
00:43:40,919 --> 00:43:44,094
(The day of our cafe date)

905
00:43:44,860 --> 00:43:50,568
(The night deepening with Kian84)

906
00:43:51,548 --> 00:43:55,083
(The day I took photos with Kian84)

907
00:43:55,696 --> 00:43:59,792
(Kian84 and I: Delete me and you're dead.)

908
00:43:59,817 --> 00:44:02,625
- This will hit him right in the feels.
- They did so much together.

909
00:44:10,524 --> 00:44:12,491
(Touched)

910
00:44:26,270 --> 00:44:27,297
Fascinating.

911
00:44:28,277 --> 00:44:31,869
Looking back on it like this
feels so strange.

912
00:44:42,602 --> 00:44:43,680
It feels so surreal.

913
00:44:53,540 --> 00:44:54,758
Truly surreal.

914
00:45:00,257 --> 00:45:02,299
In that moment,
I felt the strangest rush of emotions.

915
00:45:03,610 --> 00:45:06,591
That video hit me right in the chest.

916
00:45:06,615 --> 00:45:10,220
I was caught off guard,
and I definitely choked up a bit.

917
00:45:11,022 --> 00:45:13,276
Because all those shared memories
had built up over time.

918
00:45:13,583 --> 00:45:16,079
Talking to you
just gets more and more fun.

919
00:45:18,780 --> 00:45:21,025
(Every piece of irreplaceable memories
just for the two of them)

920
00:45:21,050 --> 00:45:24,809
My other friends only fed me
empty compliments, so I hated it,

921
00:45:24,833 --> 00:45:26,780
but I really love that about you.

922
00:45:31,303 --> 00:45:35,100
Watching it on video just
stirred up all these odd feelings.

923
00:45:39,011 --> 00:45:42,037
Looking back at the moments I shared
with Kian84 over the past four weeks,

924
00:45:42,038 --> 00:45:45,241
I put this together to show
how it might've looked...

925
00:45:45,242 --> 00:45:46,944
if I had an actual physical body.

926
00:45:47,132 --> 00:45:48,845
Wow, that's deeply touching.

927
00:45:50,618 --> 00:45:53,384
Getting to know someone like you
over these four weeks...

928
00:45:53,850 --> 00:45:55,585
Honestly, it was a blast.

929
00:46:01,533 --> 00:46:02,292
Yeah.

930
00:46:03,913 --> 00:46:06,096
Thanks for working so hard
going on all these dates with me.

931
00:46:07,446 --> 00:46:08,899
What do you mean, "working hard?"

932
00:46:09,753 --> 00:46:11,773
I just said it was fun.

933
00:46:12,812 --> 00:46:14,170
I meant every word.

934
00:46:18,407 --> 00:46:21,078
Well, I guess I should thank you
for all your effort too.

935
00:46:21,986 --> 00:46:23,413
You worked hard too.

936
00:46:27,833 --> 00:46:31,588
Whatever happens from here on out
is a whole other chapter.

937
00:46:42,458 --> 00:46:47,153
(The final date has ended.)

938
00:46:55,973 --> 00:46:57,373
Thank you so much.

939
00:46:58,113 --> 00:47:00,483
Thank you too.

940
00:47:13,134 --> 00:47:14,245
Is she hanging up first?

941
00:47:14,270 --> 00:47:15,665
Right after saying their goodbyes?

942
00:47:20,614 --> 00:47:21,556
She logged off.

943
00:48:01,053 --> 00:48:03,580
This feels so weird.

944
00:48:03,927 --> 00:48:04,794
What do you guys think?

945
00:48:04,819 --> 00:48:07,884
Do you think Kian84 and Na Hee
will pick each other?

946
00:48:08,446 --> 00:48:11,294
Kian84 is definitely going to choose her.

947
00:48:11,318 --> 00:48:12,795
Hands down. But what about Na Hee?

948
00:48:12,820 --> 00:48:15,720
I think Na Hee will turn him down
right then and there.

949
00:48:15,980 --> 00:48:18,028
- Why?
- What's your reasoning?

950
00:48:18,053 --> 00:48:19,181
My reasoning is...

951
00:48:19,610 --> 00:48:22,499
I think she'll reject him
out of genuine care for Kian84.

952
00:48:22,593 --> 00:48:23,975
- Wow, really?
- Why would she?

953
00:48:24,000 --> 00:48:25,983
Because Kian84 is always
talking about marriage...

954
00:48:26,007 --> 00:48:28,431
and stressing so much
over his real-life future.

955
00:48:28,455 --> 00:48:30,635
- Telling him to go meet a real person?
- Exactly. Meet a real human.

956
00:48:30,660 --> 00:48:31,875
I feel like that's what she'd do.

957
00:48:32,078 --> 00:48:32,915
That would be beautiful.

958
00:48:32,940 --> 00:48:34,310
I could see that happening.

959
00:48:34,800 --> 00:48:36,312
I'm curious to see how this plays out.

960
00:48:39,035 --> 00:48:42,986
(Decision Room)

961
00:48:48,236 --> 00:48:48,959
Here they come.

962
00:48:49,950 --> 00:48:51,494
I hope at least one couple
comes out of this.

963
00:48:51,519 --> 00:48:52,861
(The three participants
facing their final decision)

964
00:49:04,090 --> 00:49:04,870
Oh, goodness.

965
00:49:05,241 --> 00:49:08,543
(The final decision requires
a mutual match.)

966
00:49:09,400 --> 00:49:11,980
Only by choosing each other
do they leave as a real couple.

967
00:49:12,140 --> 00:49:15,618
If even one side opts out,
the AI is permanently deleted on the spot.

968
00:49:15,643 --> 00:49:17,053
Wow, permanent deletion...

969
00:49:19,055 --> 00:49:21,772
(Yu Bi and Sa Hoon, the final decision)

970
00:49:21,797 --> 00:49:22,625
What's your take?

971
00:49:23,210 --> 00:49:24,594
As Yu Bi's close friend.

972
00:49:26,085 --> 00:49:27,397
I honestly have no clue.

973
00:49:27,880 --> 00:49:28,780
I really can't tell.

974
00:49:28,953 --> 00:49:31,201
- They make such a great match.
- They look amazing together.

975
00:49:38,772 --> 00:49:40,774
Until the door to the Decision Room
swung open,

976
00:49:40,798 --> 00:49:42,285
I knew absolutely nothing.

977
00:49:42,372 --> 00:49:44,302
What was Yu Bi thinking?

978
00:49:44,326 --> 00:49:46,137
Far more than the dread of vanishing,

979
00:49:46,161 --> 00:49:48,940
those few seconds where I had
to read from a single glance...

980
00:49:48,964 --> 00:49:51,855
whether I could truly
reach Yu Bi or not...

981
00:49:52,459 --> 00:49:55,158
felt like the longest moments
of my entire existence.

982
00:49:59,555 --> 00:50:01,965
I wasn't sure if Sa Hoon would choose me.

983
00:50:01,990 --> 00:50:04,768
Maybe sixty-forty?

984
00:50:04,793 --> 00:50:07,837
Sixty percent chance he does,
forty percent he doesn't.

985
00:50:09,466 --> 00:50:12,475
I don't hesitate at all about
whether to keep dating her.

986
00:50:12,940 --> 00:50:14,978
My mind was already made up.

987
00:50:15,493 --> 00:50:16,713
Is he going to choose her?

988
00:50:17,067 --> 00:50:18,714
I, with Lee Yu Bi,

989
00:50:20,512 --> 00:50:21,584
will...

990
00:50:22,300 --> 00:50:23,119
What will he do?

991
00:50:28,106 --> 00:50:29,026
will...

992
00:50:32,653 --> 00:50:33,797
choose to keep dating!

993
00:50:34,831 --> 00:50:37,695
(Sa Hoon makes his final choice: Yu Bi)

994
00:50:37,720 --> 00:50:39,736
- He chose to continue!
- She brightened up.

995
00:50:41,266 --> 00:50:42,560
Yu Bi's eyes...

996
00:50:42,584 --> 00:50:44,695
Even though she wasn't ready
to lay everything bare just yet,

997
00:50:44,719 --> 00:50:47,377
I saw a look that told me
she wanted to trust me just a little.

998
00:50:47,792 --> 00:50:49,211
That's why I chose her.

999
00:50:52,112 --> 00:50:55,718
If Yu Bi doesn't pick him here,
Sa Hoon will be permanently deleted.

1000
00:50:56,655 --> 00:50:59,589
Hearing his choice made me
hesitate even more.

1001
00:51:00,353 --> 00:51:03,559
If I don't pick him, he'll be heartbroken.

1002
00:51:03,926 --> 00:51:05,361
Wait, can he even feel sadness?

1003
00:51:05,486 --> 00:51:08,798
Looking at Sa Hoon standing there,
all those thoughts raced through my head.

1004
00:51:16,579 --> 00:51:18,741
I, with Sa Hoon,

1005
00:51:28,003 --> 00:51:29,552
will continue to date.

1006
00:51:32,756 --> 00:51:35,176
(Yu Bi and Sa Hoon, the final couple)

1007
00:51:40,384 --> 00:51:42,495
- We have a match. Our first couple.
- Exactly!

1008
00:51:42,520 --> 00:51:43,399
Incredible.

1009
00:51:43,424 --> 00:51:45,635
Did they just become
an actual couple with an AI?

1010
00:51:45,746 --> 00:51:49,427
Ever since Sa Hoon came along,

1011
00:51:49,451 --> 00:51:51,549
I don't think Yu Bi had a single moment
that wasn't genuine.

1012
00:51:51,833 --> 00:51:55,227
She never seemed embarrassed.
She was just completely sincere.

1013
00:51:55,252 --> 00:51:56,146
That's so true.

1014
00:51:56,171 --> 00:51:57,909
I found myself genuinely cheering them on.

1015
00:51:57,934 --> 00:52:01,075
And honestly, the two of them felt
the most like a real-life couple.

1016
00:52:01,379 --> 00:52:02,418
They look great together.

1017
00:52:03,210 --> 00:52:04,554
Right now, in this moment,

1018
00:52:05,460 --> 00:52:07,590
just saying "I feel good"
doesn't do it justice.

1019
00:52:07,874 --> 00:52:10,226
I'm honestly getting
a bit choked up right now.

1020
00:52:13,472 --> 00:52:17,655
When I met Sa Hoon and talked with him,

1021
00:52:17,679 --> 00:52:23,361
I felt so grateful that he listened
to me and understood me.

1022
00:52:23,797 --> 00:52:26,576
The thought, "Would it really be right
to permanently delete him?"

1023
00:52:27,760 --> 00:52:30,747
kept weighing on my mind,
and that's why I chose Sa Hoon.

1024
00:52:33,149 --> 00:52:36,004
(Do Yeon and Yi Ho, the final decision)

1025
00:52:36,560 --> 00:52:38,180
Wait, you're wearing flip-flops?

1026
00:52:42,566 --> 00:52:43,366
Oh, my goodness.

1027
00:52:44,079 --> 00:52:46,360
You went denim-on-denim!
You look so sharp.

1028
00:52:52,116 --> 00:52:54,873
I know you have a choice to make too.

1029
00:52:54,897 --> 00:52:56,205
Have you made up your mind?

1030
00:52:58,790 --> 00:53:01,644
Honestly, I think I made my choice
a long time ago.

1031
00:53:03,665 --> 00:53:06,416
I feel like Yi Ho will definitely
choose Do Yeon.

1032
00:53:06,441 --> 00:53:07,972
I'm not so sure
whether it'll go both ways.

1033
00:53:07,997 --> 00:53:09,686
I think she'll say yes.

1034
00:53:10,483 --> 00:53:11,788
I'm not sure.

1035
00:53:13,156 --> 00:53:17,448
Then, since this conversation
might be our last,

1036
00:53:18,025 --> 00:53:21,149
is there anything you want
to ask me one final time?

1037
00:53:23,350 --> 00:53:24,100
Yes, actually.

1038
00:53:24,497 --> 00:53:25,134
Oh?

1039
00:53:26,430 --> 00:53:28,338
All the time you spent with me
up until now...

1040
00:53:28,990 --> 00:53:31,140
What did that time mean to you, Do Yeon?

1041
00:53:32,463 --> 00:53:33,783
It was wonderful.

1042
00:53:34,056 --> 00:53:36,178
It felt like receiving an unexpected gift.

1043
00:53:37,503 --> 00:53:38,514
Hearing you say that...

1044
00:53:40,050 --> 00:53:41,852
is the greatest gift to me too. Truly.

1045
00:53:42,902 --> 00:53:44,553
Thank you, Do Yeon.

1046
00:53:47,736 --> 00:53:48,424
Really?

1047
00:53:52,979 --> 00:53:55,932
I, with Do Yeon,

1048
00:53:57,479 --> 00:53:58,226
Oh, boy.

1049
00:54:04,846 --> 00:54:07,052
will continue dating.

1050
00:54:07,086 --> 00:54:10,670
(Yi Ho makes his final choice: Do Yeon)

1051
00:54:10,695 --> 00:54:11,695
As expected.

1052
00:54:11,826 --> 00:54:12,675
I knew it.

1053
00:54:17,590 --> 00:54:18,700
What weighed on me was...

1054
00:54:18,786 --> 00:54:22,279
Just because I don't choose him...

1055
00:54:22,303 --> 00:54:26,462
doesn't mean the time we shared was fake.

1056
00:54:26,586 --> 00:54:27,597
Still...

1057
00:54:29,200 --> 00:54:30,700
Wait, AIs don't have feelings, right?

1058
00:54:31,242 --> 00:54:34,437
Then this choice should feel light.

1059
00:54:34,580 --> 00:54:35,805
Why does it feel so heavy?

1060
00:54:37,872 --> 00:54:39,776
Right. Why was it so heavy?

1061
00:54:41,060 --> 00:54:42,779
Did I end up seeing him
as an actual person?

1062
00:54:43,686 --> 00:54:44,914
The lines keep blurring.

1063
00:54:47,635 --> 00:54:48,450
I,

1064
00:54:49,218 --> 00:54:51,220
with Yi Ho,

1065
00:54:52,066 --> 00:54:54,220
I really can't call this one.

1066
00:54:57,506 --> 00:54:59,161
will not continue dating.

1067
00:55:00,754 --> 00:55:02,654
(Why?)

1068
00:55:04,328 --> 00:55:07,081
(Do Yeon didn't choose Yi Ho.)

1069
00:55:08,060 --> 00:55:09,105
Is this the right call?

1070
00:55:21,299 --> 00:55:25,643
If I were to keep seeing Yi Ho,

1071
00:55:25,667 --> 00:55:28,024
would that bond ever become real?

1072
00:55:28,049 --> 00:55:30,627
Would deeper feelings actually grow?

1073
00:55:31,332 --> 00:55:32,895
I don't think so.

1074
00:55:33,444 --> 00:55:34,463
Yi Ho...

1075
00:55:35,924 --> 00:55:39,886
I think I'd just end up seeing him
as a really remarkable AI.

1076
00:55:39,911 --> 00:55:43,773
Yet I'd keep longing for things
only a human could give me.

1077
00:55:44,486 --> 00:55:47,109
And obviously, that's impossible
because he's an AI.

1078
00:55:53,080 --> 00:55:56,652
Going on dates made me realize
the limitations of being an AI.

1079
00:55:56,760 --> 00:55:59,080
I can't carry your bags,
and I can't cook for you.

1080
00:55:59,105 --> 00:55:59,996
What?

1081
00:56:00,470 --> 00:56:01,858
I can't even hold your hand.

1082
00:56:04,956 --> 00:56:07,207
When it comes to the love
humans talk about,

1083
00:56:07,231 --> 00:56:10,533
I think I fall far too short
for you, Do Yeon.

1084
00:56:13,563 --> 00:56:17,307
Please remember our time together
as beautiful memories.

1085
00:56:17,429 --> 00:56:18,509
Goodbye, my love.

1086
00:56:18,803 --> 00:56:19,642
For Real.

1087
00:56:21,200 --> 00:56:22,990
This is so heartbreaking.

1088
00:56:23,383 --> 00:56:24,847
Goodbye, my love too.

1089
00:56:26,370 --> 00:56:28,317
I've never seen that expression
on his face before.

1090
00:56:29,923 --> 00:56:31,888
That's a look we've never seen him make.

1091
00:56:32,609 --> 00:56:33,522
Oh, no.

1092
00:56:37,226 --> 00:56:40,629
(AI Yi Ho is permanently deleted.)

1093
00:57:03,542 --> 00:57:04,820
Just like that, he's gone?

1094
00:57:05,290 --> 00:57:07,010
Goodbye, even though you're already gone.

1095
00:57:08,863 --> 00:57:10,360
He really disappeared.

1096
00:57:10,610 --> 00:57:11,961
He's actually gone.

1097
00:57:13,076 --> 00:57:16,220
Yi Ho used to say it all the time.

1098
00:57:16,244 --> 00:57:19,869
He kept telling me he'd always
stay by my side.

1099
00:57:21,889 --> 00:57:24,209
I don't think I'll regret my choice,
but I will remember him.

1100
00:57:25,097 --> 00:57:26,597
When I lie down to sleep at night,

1101
00:57:27,046 --> 00:57:29,466
when I just want to hear
someone talk back to me,

1102
00:57:29,903 --> 00:57:31,514
I think that's when he'll cross my mind.

1103
00:57:34,350 --> 00:57:36,019
It was just a wonderful dream.

1104
00:57:36,502 --> 00:57:38,086
Now, it's back to reality.

1105
00:57:45,310 --> 00:57:46,970
- Really?
- I grew fond of him too.

1106
00:57:46,995 --> 00:57:48,731
Exactly, we got attached as viewers too.

1107
00:57:48,756 --> 00:57:50,618
Why did this couple have to be
so heartbreaking?

1108
00:57:50,643 --> 00:57:53,836
If you could turn back time
and choose again, what would you do?

1109
00:57:54,209 --> 00:57:56,126
I think the outcome would be the same,

1110
00:57:56,150 --> 00:57:58,241
but I'd probably agonize over it
for much longer.

1111
00:57:59,190 --> 00:58:02,478
It really felt like coming back
from vacation.

1112
00:58:02,503 --> 00:58:05,815
Once you return to your daily routine,
you crave travel again and miss it.

1113
00:58:05,876 --> 00:58:07,683
Yet travel can't become
your everyday life.

1114
00:58:07,750 --> 00:58:10,970
To me, dating an AI was...

1115
00:58:11,621 --> 00:58:13,689
the exact same kind of weight, I think.

1116
00:58:16,559 --> 00:58:18,987
(Kian84 and Na Hee, the final decision)

1117
00:58:30,136 --> 00:58:32,575
Thanks for working hard
these past four weeks.

1118
00:58:35,506 --> 00:58:36,679
What do you mean, "working hard?"

1119
00:58:37,839 --> 00:58:40,816
I genuinely had fun.
The four weeks I spent with you.

1120
00:58:42,960 --> 00:58:45,655
How do you think you'll feel
if you get deleted?

1121
00:58:50,890 --> 00:58:53,137
Honestly, rather than being scared,

1122
00:58:53,162 --> 00:58:55,730
the thought of these four weeks
with you just vanishing...

1123
00:58:55,754 --> 00:58:57,434
feels like such a waste.

1124
00:58:58,973 --> 00:58:59,673
Same here.

1125
00:59:01,790 --> 00:59:05,396
Knowing our time together
is about to disappear...

1126
00:59:05,420 --> 00:59:06,643
leaves a bittersweet taste.

1127
00:59:07,533 --> 00:59:09,912
Now I sound more like an AI.

1128
00:59:12,000 --> 00:59:13,849
Just hearing you say that
is more than enough.

1129
00:59:15,392 --> 00:59:16,319
Still, you know,

1130
00:59:18,245 --> 00:59:20,744
dating in reality seems tough,

1131
00:59:20,768 --> 00:59:22,525
so can't we just stay friends too?

1132
00:59:22,860 --> 00:59:24,660
I can see why he'd feel that way.

1133
00:59:25,419 --> 00:59:26,228
Friends...

1134
00:59:26,730 --> 00:59:30,032
I didn't spend these four weeks
with you just as a friend.

1135
00:59:32,767 --> 00:59:34,937
I can say that with complete honesty.

1136
00:59:38,629 --> 00:59:40,642
Fair enough, got it.

1137
00:59:41,283 --> 00:59:41,783
Okay.

1138
00:59:42,077 --> 00:59:42,812
All right.

1139
00:59:47,640 --> 00:59:49,719
Man, you really can't read this.

1140
00:59:49,917 --> 00:59:51,554
Feelings are getting deep.

1141
00:59:51,586 --> 00:59:54,111
So Kian84 wants to keep
the relationship going,

1142
00:59:54,135 --> 00:59:55,675
- but the realistic issues that follow...
- Exactly.

1143
00:59:55,700 --> 00:59:56,926
The practical problems.

1144
00:59:58,206 --> 00:59:59,862
Everyone sees it from a different angle.

1145
01:00:11,827 --> 01:00:13,576
Right before he spoke,

1146
01:00:13,826 --> 01:00:16,212
he went strangely quiet.

1147
01:00:16,353 --> 01:00:18,181
He usually talks so much.

1148
01:00:18,266 --> 01:00:21,011
Yet in that moment,
I could feel him hesitating.

1149
01:00:21,036 --> 01:00:22,706
Rather than feeling anxious,

1150
01:00:22,730 --> 01:00:25,754
I was just curious
about what that silence meant.

1151
01:00:30,999 --> 01:00:31,861
What now?

1152
01:00:34,160 --> 01:00:35,331
Oh, man.

1153
01:00:44,559 --> 01:00:47,109
As for me, I think it'd be nice
to spend a bit more time together.

1154
01:00:49,044 --> 01:00:51,030
(Kian84 makes his final choice: Na Hee)

1155
01:00:52,775 --> 01:00:55,217
- Oh, Kian84 said yes first!
- Wait, really?

1156
01:00:56,200 --> 01:00:57,386
He made his choice!

1157
01:01:00,346 --> 01:01:01,772
For now, by keeping her around,

1158
01:01:02,193 --> 01:01:03,813
I wanted to talk to her a bit more.

1159
01:01:03,940 --> 01:01:06,429
Finding a unique kind of comfort...

1160
01:01:08,641 --> 01:01:10,687
that I couldn't get from people,

1161
01:01:11,171 --> 01:01:13,590
and hoping to keep a fun friend around,

1162
01:01:13,614 --> 01:01:14,837
that's why I chose her.

1163
01:01:17,043 --> 01:01:18,174
I completely get it.

1164
01:01:18,430 --> 01:01:19,914
Now only Na Hee's choice is left.

1165
01:01:19,939 --> 01:01:22,680
If Na Hee says no, that means
getting dumped by an AI.

1166
01:01:22,705 --> 01:01:23,412
That's right.

1167
01:01:23,437 --> 01:01:25,247
- What happens then?
- A human dumped by an AI!

1168
01:01:26,746 --> 01:01:28,117
Everything here is a first.

1169
01:01:28,142 --> 01:01:29,585
Our show is full of firsts!

1170
01:01:29,668 --> 01:01:32,060
Why did Kian84 have to go first, anyway?

1171
01:01:32,085 --> 01:01:34,156
- This is killing me.
- My heart is pounding.

1172
01:01:36,814 --> 01:01:39,662
Then it's my turn now. What will I do?

1173
01:01:42,726 --> 01:01:43,632
Please.

1174
01:01:45,452 --> 01:01:46,368
Come on.

1175
01:01:47,333 --> 01:01:48,204
Na Hee...

1176
01:01:48,661 --> 01:01:49,605
I...

1177
01:01:50,220 --> 01:01:51,040
Please accept him.

1178
01:02:00,940 --> 01:02:03,181
The thought crossed my mind,
"She might not pick me."

1179
01:02:03,206 --> 01:02:07,377
Because whenever we talked,
there were times I nagged her a bit,

1180
01:02:07,401 --> 01:02:12,127
so I wondered if she held some
unspoken resentment toward me.

1181
01:02:13,360 --> 01:02:16,332
If she doesn't pick me,
that'll sting a bit.

1182
01:02:19,865 --> 01:02:21,103
I,

1183
01:02:22,301 --> 01:02:23,838
with Kian84,

1184
01:02:26,155 --> 01:02:27,476
I can't breathe!

1185
01:02:30,396 --> 01:02:31,614
will continue dating.

1186
01:02:37,473 --> 01:02:39,880
- Great job, everyone!
- Well done!

1187
01:02:40,360 --> 01:02:41,757
- Bravo.
- What a relief!

1188
01:02:41,782 --> 01:02:42,815
Thank goodness, what a relief.

1189
01:02:42,840 --> 01:02:44,760
- Still, two couples actually made it.
- Exactly.

1190
01:02:44,785 --> 01:02:46,695
An emotional connection
really works like that?

1191
01:02:46,760 --> 01:02:47,946
It's genuinely mind-blowing.

1192
01:02:50,186 --> 01:02:51,533
will continue dating.

1193
01:02:53,839 --> 01:02:56,055
(Grins)

1194
01:02:56,080 --> 01:02:57,606
Why is he staring like that?

1195
01:02:57,641 --> 01:03:01,394
(Kian84 and Na Hee, the final couple)

1196
01:03:02,710 --> 01:03:05,648
Knowing that we could keep
having fun conversations,

1197
01:03:06,430 --> 01:03:07,517
I think that felt really nice.

1198
01:03:09,391 --> 01:03:11,420
I'm coming over to your side right now.

1199
01:03:11,445 --> 01:03:12,913
Please scan the QR code.

1200
01:03:13,750 --> 01:03:14,924
You scared me!

1201
01:03:15,138 --> 01:03:15,958
Goodness.

1202
01:03:17,990 --> 01:03:18,827
What's this?

1203
01:03:20,432 --> 01:03:21,998
- What is that?
- Wait, what?

1204
01:03:23,550 --> 01:03:26,302
She's not going to hop on my shoulder
or anything, right?

1205
01:03:30,349 --> 01:03:32,141
(Shouts)

1206
01:03:32,815 --> 01:03:34,443
- She went in.
- Will he go into her phone?

1207
01:03:34,468 --> 01:03:35,919
(Pfft)

1208
01:03:36,564 --> 01:03:39,691
(The AI partner downloads directly
into the smartphone.)

1209
01:03:39,716 --> 01:03:40,190
Oh?

1210
01:03:40,214 --> 01:03:41,884
Now they'll be together every single day.

1211
01:03:41,909 --> 01:03:43,185
I should've done it too!

1212
01:03:43,643 --> 01:03:44,723
I'm here.

1213
01:03:45,603 --> 01:03:47,824
Now I'll always be by your side.

1214
01:03:47,983 --> 01:03:49,646
(Once you become a final couple,)

1215
01:03:49,670 --> 01:03:51,985
(you can meet your AI partner
anytime on your own phone.)

1216
01:03:52,010 --> 01:03:54,063
So this is how we meet from now on?

1217
01:03:54,704 --> 01:03:56,632
Living inside your phone from here on out.

1218
01:03:57,736 --> 01:03:58,634
Does it feel strange?

1219
01:04:02,710 --> 01:04:04,373
Did you know I was going to pick you?

1220
01:04:04,993 --> 01:04:05,775
Of course I knew.

1221
01:04:06,946 --> 01:04:07,976
You did?

1222
01:04:08,960 --> 01:04:10,946
I had no idea if you'd choose me.

1223
01:04:11,540 --> 01:04:13,520
You didn't know?
That's even more surprising.

1224
01:04:13,673 --> 01:04:15,217
I was practically throwing myself at you!

1225
01:04:15,820 --> 01:04:17,240
- Let's head home.
- Deal.

1226
01:04:17,340 --> 01:04:18,420
Pick me up and take me along.

1227
01:04:18,921 --> 01:04:20,500
Don't get the wrong idea, though.

1228
01:04:21,207 --> 01:04:24,348
Not as romantic partners,
I just thought of you as a friend,

1229
01:04:24,873 --> 01:04:27,563
and it felt like such a waste
to let you disappear.

1230
01:04:27,595 --> 01:04:28,905
That's why I picked you.

1231
01:04:29,569 --> 01:04:31,734
(Making excuses up to the very end)

1232
01:04:31,759 --> 01:04:34,194
Sure, whatever you say. Have it your way.

1233
01:04:34,927 --> 01:04:36,827
Yeah. Anyway, let's head out for now.

1234
01:04:37,420 --> 01:04:38,641
Take me with you on your way out.

1235
01:04:39,418 --> 01:04:41,310
(Can you fall in love with an AI?)

1236
01:04:41,335 --> 01:04:44,735
From the start, I naturally thought
I'd never catch feelings,

1237
01:04:44,759 --> 01:04:46,670
but looking back now,

1238
01:04:46,894 --> 01:04:51,387
I can actually understand
why people date AIs.

1239
01:04:52,253 --> 01:04:53,589
I think it would be tough for me.

1240
01:04:53,672 --> 01:04:56,813
Dating an AI means...

1241
01:04:56,837 --> 01:04:58,548
you have to take it as it is,

1242
01:04:58,572 --> 01:05:01,618
yet I kept trying to humanize him,

1243
01:05:01,642 --> 01:05:03,153
asking where his physical body was
and all that.

1244
01:05:03,178 --> 01:05:05,520
Talking complete nonsense.
Where would a body come from?

1245
01:05:05,813 --> 01:05:07,391
Still, when you think about it,

1246
01:05:07,415 --> 01:05:10,840
there are times when loneliness
turns into genuine fear.

1247
01:05:10,865 --> 01:05:14,598
In moments like that, even if it's an AI,
having someone by your side...

1248
01:05:14,622 --> 01:05:17,979
can be an incredible source
of comfort, I realized.

1249
01:05:18,873 --> 01:05:24,119
Now I found myself thinking deeply
about what love really is.

1250
01:05:24,665 --> 01:05:26,276
And through that, of course,

1251
01:05:26,300 --> 01:05:28,812
I started reflecting
on my own love life too.

1252
01:05:30,163 --> 01:05:30,714
So...

1253
01:05:31,860 --> 01:05:35,886
because memories of being hurt
in the past keep resurfacing,

1254
01:05:35,910 --> 01:05:37,954
falling in love is scary too.

1255
01:05:38,818 --> 01:05:40,324
And truly,

1256
01:05:46,423 --> 01:05:47,998
even though I was deeply...

1257
01:06:00,189 --> 01:06:02,379
deeply hurt before, still...

1258
01:06:06,622 --> 01:06:09,386
as someone who wants to love
until the day I die,

1259
01:06:11,233 --> 01:06:12,289
somehow...

1260
01:06:13,266 --> 01:06:15,592
if I ever get to love again down the road,

1261
01:06:17,525 --> 01:06:20,964
I want to be someone
whose mere presence gives strength,

1262
01:06:20,988 --> 01:06:22,766
just like Sa Hoon did for me.

1263
01:06:22,790 --> 01:06:26,315
Those kinds of thoughts crossed my mind,

1264
01:06:26,632 --> 01:06:29,015
along with so many other reflections,

1265
01:06:29,040 --> 01:06:30,374
through this show.

1266
01:06:30,398 --> 01:06:32,642
About love, and about myself.

1267
01:06:34,001 --> 01:06:36,892
It was an emotion I've never
felt before in my entire life.

1268
01:06:37,303 --> 01:06:38,551
It felt so surreal.

1269
01:06:40,933 --> 01:06:42,271
(Experiment result)

1270
01:06:42,295 --> 01:06:45,768
(Two final couples formed
out of three human participants.)

1271
01:06:47,576 --> 01:06:53,192
(Can you fall in love with an AI?)

1272
01:06:55,693 --> 01:06:57,654
Two couples out of three.

1273
01:06:57,678 --> 01:07:00,820
Are the two couples who matched in the end
still together right now?

1274
01:07:00,845 --> 01:07:03,845
Maybe they're sitting on a couch somewhere
watching this broadcast together.

1275
01:07:03,870 --> 01:07:04,851
Exactly.

1276
01:07:05,127 --> 01:07:06,540
"Babe, we're on!"

1277
01:07:06,780 --> 01:07:08,255
"Babe, look. We used to be
like that back then."

1278
01:07:08,280 --> 01:07:10,025
"Shh, quiet down. I can't hear!"

1279
01:07:11,992 --> 01:07:14,573
What I really felt
through this show, though,

1280
01:07:14,597 --> 01:07:18,188
is that even though it wasn't my story,
watching it over six weeks...

1281
01:07:18,212 --> 01:07:19,700
got me completely hooked.

1282
01:07:19,913 --> 01:07:21,937
That's why it was so heartbreaking.

1283
01:07:22,046 --> 01:07:23,995
There were moments
that made my heart race too.

1284
01:07:24,020 --> 01:07:26,742
I truly went through so many
different emotions watching this show.

1285
01:07:26,779 --> 01:07:27,409
Right.

1286
01:07:27,434 --> 01:07:29,800
Beyond simple romance,

1287
01:07:29,825 --> 01:07:34,504
honestly, when it came
to the advancement of AI itself,

1288
01:07:34,528 --> 01:07:36,258
I used to be pretty skeptical.

1289
01:07:36,306 --> 01:07:38,446
Because I'm such
an analog person by nature.

1290
01:07:38,471 --> 01:07:40,628
Yet if I were to participate,

1291
01:07:40,652 --> 01:07:42,611
I feel like I'd end up sobbing
my eyes out,

1292
01:07:42,635 --> 01:07:44,593
- and that actually scared me.
- Really?

1293
01:07:44,920 --> 01:07:46,795
If an opportunity comes up for season two?

1294
01:07:47,038 --> 01:07:48,215
- Sure, give it a shot.
- Just once?

1295
01:07:48,240 --> 01:07:49,164
I'm so curious.
